NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware lets you hook into every stage of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" lifecycle — from configuration to streaming, tool execution, usage tracking, and completion. You can observe, transform, or short-circuit behavior at each stage without modifying your adapter or tool implementations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common use cases include:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logging and observability"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — track token usage, tool execution timing, errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration transforms"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — inject system prompts, adjust temperature per iteration, filter tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream processing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — redact sensitive content, transform chunks, drop unwanted events"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool call interception"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — validate arguments, cache results, abort on dangerous calls"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Side effects"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — send analytics, update databases, trigger notifications"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an array of middleware to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst logger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"logger\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Chat started`);\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Finished in ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [logger],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Just want to see chunks flowing through your middleware during development?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nUse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug: { middleware: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" on your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call — no custom middleware required. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./debug-logging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Logging"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lifecycle-overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" invocation follows a predictable lifecycle. Middleware hooks fire at specific phases:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"graph TD\n    A[\"chat() called\"] --> B[\"onConfig (phase: init)\"]\n    B --> C[onStart]\n    C --> D[\"onConfig (phase: beforeModel)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Adapter streams response\"]\n    E --> F[\"onChunk (for each chunk)\"]\n    F --> G{Tool calls?}\n    G -->|No| H[onUsage]\n    G -->|Yes| I[onBeforeToolCall]\n    I --> J[Tool executes]\n    J --> K[onAfterToolCall]\n    K --> L{Continue loop?}\n    L -->|Yes| D\n    L -->|No| H\n    H --> SO{\"Structured output path?\"}\n    SO -->|None| M{Outcome}\n    SO -->|\"Native combined\"| SOH[\"Post-loop structured-output harvest (onChunk)\"]\n    SOH --> M\n    SO -->|\"Separate finalization\"| SOC[onStructuredOutputConfig]\n    SOC --> SOM[\"onConfig (phase: structuredOutput)\"]\n    SOM --> SOS[\"Structured-output finalization (onChunk, onUsage)\"]\n    SOS --> M\n    M -->|Success| N[onFinish]\n    M -->|Abort| O[onAbort]\n    M -->|Error| P[onError]\n\n    style I fill:#e1f5ff\n    style J fill:#ffe1e1\n    style SOC fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOM fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOS fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOH fill:#e1f5ff\n    style N fill:#e1ffe1\n    style O fill:#fff4e1\n    style P fill:#ffe1e1","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"phase-transitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Phase Transitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The context's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase"},{"type":"text","value":" field tracks where you are in the lifecycle:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Phase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hooks Called"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"init"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once at startup"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before each model call (per iteration)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelStream"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While adapter streams chunks"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before tool execution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After tool execution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During the final structured-output adapter call (when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" is set "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for the current model/options). Chunks from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter.structuredOutputStream"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the synthesized non-streaming fallback) flow through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" with this phase, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" fires for the final call's tokens. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Does not fire"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for adapters that natively combine tools + schema in one streaming call (modern OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x family, and OpenRouter when every routed model is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_COMBINED_TOOLS_AND_SCHEMA_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":"; see issue #605). On that path middleware observes the run through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelStream"},{"type":"text","value":" as usual."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hooks-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hooks Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onconfig","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onConfig"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called once during "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"init"},{"type":"text","value":" (startup) and once per iteration during "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":" (before each model call). On the separate-finalization path, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" additionally re-fires at the structured-output boundary with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'"},{"type":"text","value":", receiving the post-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" view of the config. A single-iteration separate-finalization run therefore fires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" three times ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"init"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutput"},{"type":"text","value":"). Native-combined output does not add this third call. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" to transform the configuration that the model receives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"partial"}]},{"type":"text","value":" config object with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config automatically. No need to spread the existing config."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst dynamicTemperature: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"dynamic-temperature\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase === \"init\") {\n      // Add a system prompt at startup — only systemPrompts is overwritten\n      return {\n        systemPrompts: [\n          ...config.systemPrompts,\n          \"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n        ],\n      };\n    }\n\n    if (ctx.phase === \"beforeModel\" && ctx.iteration > 0) {\n      // Increase temperature on retries. Sampling params live in the\n      // provider-native modelOptions object — `temperature` is universal,\n      // so it's the same key across providers. Spread the existing\n      // modelOptions so other model options stay unchanged.\n      const current =\n        typeof config.modelOptions?.temperature === \"number\"\n          ? config.modelOptions.temperature\n          : 0.7;\n      return {\n        modelOptions: {\n          ...config.modelOptions,\n          temperature: Math.min(current + 0.1, 1.0),\n        },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sampling parameters ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", the various "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max*Tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" keys) live inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" under each provider's native name — they are no longer root config fields. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":" happens to be spelled the same across every provider, so the example above is provider-agnostic; if you mutate a token limit instead, use the provider-native key (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" for OpenAI, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"num_predict"},{"type":"text","value":" nested under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options"},{"type":"text","value":" for Ollama). See "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Config fields you can transform:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ModelMessage[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canonical conversation history. Persistence and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" use this field."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerMessages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ModelMessage[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporary context sent to the provider. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"System prompts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tool[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available tools"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Request metadata"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-native options — this is where sampling params ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", the provider's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max*Tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When multiple middleware define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", the config is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"piped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerMessages"},{"type":"text","value":" when a transform must affect only the model call. For\ncompatibility, returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" also updates provider input unless the same\nresult sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerMessages"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onstructuredoutputconfig","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called once at the start of the final structured-output adapter call — only when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" was invoked with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for the current model/options. Pipes through middleware in order, like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", but with access to the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON Schema"}]},{"type":"text","value":" being sent to the provider. Use this hook when you need to transform the schema (e.g., inject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$defs"},{"type":"text","value":", strip vendor-incompatible keywords) or apply structured-output-specific behavior (e.g., suppress system prompts on the final call)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native-combined adapters (modern OpenAI, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605) skip the separate finalization call and never invoke this hook. The engine passes the converted schema directly to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" runs, so middleware cannot transform the native-combined schema."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"partial"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config. Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":" to pass through."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { sharedDefs } from \"./defs\";\n\nconst injectDefs: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"inject-defs\",\n  onStructuredOutputConfig: (_ctx, config) => {\n    // `config.outputSchema` is the JSON Schema being sent to the provider\n    return {\n      outputSchema: {\n        ...config.outputSchema,\n        $defs: { ...sharedDefs },\n      },\n    };\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Config fields you can transform:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ModelMessage[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canonical conversation history"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerMessages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ModelMessage[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporary context sent to the final call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SystemPrompt[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"System prompts on the final call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Request metadata"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-native options — this is where sampling params ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", the provider's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max*Tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSONSchema"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON Schema being sent to the provider for structured output"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordering at the structured-output boundary:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" fires first, piping through every middleware in array order."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" then re-fires at the same boundary with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'"},{"type":"text","value":", receiving the post-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" view of the config (minus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":"). Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" for general-purpose transforms that apply to every adapter call; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" when you need access to the schema."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When multiple middleware define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", the config is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"piped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onstart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onStart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called once after the initial "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" completes. Use it for setup tasks like initializing timers or logging."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timer: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timer\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`Request ${ctx.requestId} started at iteration ${ctx.iteration}`);\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onchunk","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onChunk"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called for every chunk streamed from the adapter. You can observe, transform, expand, or drop chunks."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactor: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redactor\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      // Transform: redact sensitive content\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Return void to pass through unchanged\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return values:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chunk passes through unchanged"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replaces the original chunk"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expands into multiple chunks"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drops the chunk entirely"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When multiple middleware define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":", chunks flow through them in order. If one middleware drops a chunk (returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"), subsequent middleware never see it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"chunk-types-you-ll-see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chunk types you'll see"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" receives every "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI event"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the run produces — not just text. Narrow on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type"},{"type":"text","value":" (a discriminated union) before reading type-specific fields. The common ones:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key fields"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run lifecycle boundaries"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage"},{"type":"text","value":" (on finish), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":" (on error)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_START"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_END"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assistant text streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messageId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delta"},{"type":"text","value":" (content)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_START"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_END"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool invocation streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallName"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delta"},{"type":"text","value":" (args), result on end"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking / reasoning steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STATE_SNAPSHOT"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STATE_DELTA"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent state sync"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshot"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delta"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extensibility events (incl. structured-output — see below)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI protocol docs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full event catalogue and exact field shapes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"transforming-structured-output-chunks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transforming structured-output chunks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — and you don't need one. When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" is invoked with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", the structured-output chunks (the JSON "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":" deltas, plus the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.start"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM events and any finalization "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":") flow through the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":" as everything else. You transform, expand, or drop them exactly like any other chunk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How you distinguish them depends on which finalization path the adapter takes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Separate-finalization adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for the current model/options): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'"},{"type":"text","value":" during the finalization call. Discriminate on the phase."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native-combined adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (modern OpenAI Chat Completions / Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605): the schema-constrained JSON is produced on the model's natural final turn, so "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" stays "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'modelStream'"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'structuredOutput'"},{"type":"text","value":" phase never fires. Discriminate on the CUSTOM event name ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.start"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":") instead."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactStructuredOutput: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redact-structured-output\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    // Separate-finalization path: the JSON streams as TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\n    // during the 'structuredOutput' phase. Transform the delta like any\n    // other text chunk — here, redact anything that looks like an SSN before\n    // it reaches the client.\n    if (\n      ctx.phase === \"structuredOutput\" &&\n      chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"\n    ) {\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n\n    // Both paths: the completed typed payload arrives as a CUSTOM\n    // `structured-output.complete` event. On the native-combined path this is\n    // your only signal (ctx.phase never flips to 'structuredOutput'), so key\n    // off the event name, not the phase. `chunk.value` carries { object, raw }.\n    if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n      console.log(\"final structured output:\", chunk.value);\n    }\n\n    // Return void to pass everything else through unchanged.\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why is there "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" but no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"? Because the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"config"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shape genuinely differs at the structured-output boundary — it carries an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" field that plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn't (see "},{"type":"link","href":"#onstructuredoutputconfig","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"}]},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chunks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are all just "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" regardless of phase, so one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the CUSTOM event name) covers every case — a parallel chunk hook would be redundant."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onshouldcontinue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onShouldContinue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called when the engine is deciding whether to start another agent-loop iteration (after a tool phase or between model turns). Combined with AND semantics across middleware "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentLoopStrategy"},{"type":"text","value":" — any explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" stops the loop. Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" to allow continuation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Does "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" abort the run: the stream finishes normally with the current messages. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.abort()"},{"type":"text","value":" only for a hard abort."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst budget: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-budget\",\n  onShouldContinue: (_ctx, state) => {\n    // Stop further turns once 20 tool calls have been emitted\n    if (state.toolCallCount >= 20) return false;\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a full per-turn + cumulative tool budget recipe, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool-call budgets"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"oninterruptboundary-and-oninterruptresolution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onInterruptBoundary and onInterruptResolution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use these hooks when middleware needs data from the client. Define the request\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineInterrupt()"},{"type":"text","value":" and register it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ interrupts })"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat({ interrupts })"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not emit raw AG-UI events from middleware."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" runs at four points in an agent iteration:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":", before the adapter starts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"},{"type":"text","value":", after the model response is complete."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"},{"type":"text","value":", before tool execution starts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"},{"type":"text","value":", after the tool phase is complete."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each middleware can return requests from one boundary. The engine combines all\nrequests from that boundary into one AG-UI interrupt batch. The batch ends the\nrun with one interrupt outcome."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook cannot change config. Its only legal return is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ interrupts }"},{"type":"text","value":" or\nnothing. The continuation is a new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call, so the hook runs again. Skip\nthe emit when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is set if this pause belongs to the original\nrequest only."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx"},{"type":"text","value":" at each phase, and when to use each phase, is in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../interrupts/boundaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle Boundaries"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one shared definition. Both the server and the client import this value,\nso the definition ID and response shape stay the same on both sides."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineInterrupt, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const reviewPlan = defineInterrupt({\n  id: 'review-plan',\n  payloadSchema: z.object({ title: z.string() }),\n  responseSchema: z.object({ approved: z.boolean() }),\n})\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeTools') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'release-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Approve this plan?',\n          payload: { title: 'Release plan' },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"title=\"review-plan.ts\"","title":"review-plan.ts","file":"review-plan.ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the definition on the server. Forward "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":" so\na client resolution starts the continuation with its full context."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequestBody,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware, reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequestBody(await request.json())\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"title=\"route.ts\"","title":"route.ts","file":"route.ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the same definition on the client. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"definitionId"},{"type":"text","value":".\nTypeScript then treats the item as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the response shape from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reviewPlan.responseSchema"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { GenericInterrupt } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nfunction ReviewCard({\n  interrupt,\n}: {\n  interrupt: GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>\n}) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt({ approved: true })}\n    >\n      Approve plan\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n\nexport function ReviewPlanPanel() {\n  const { interrupts, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button onClick={() => sendMessage('Review the release plan')}>\n        Start review\n      </button>\n      {interrupts.map((interrupt) => {\n        if (interrupt.kind !== 'generic') return null\n        if (!('definitionId' in interrupt)) return null\n        if (interrupt.definitionId !== reviewPlan.id) return null\n        return <ReviewCard key={interrupt.id} interrupt={interrupt} />\n      })}\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"review-plan-panel.tsx\"","title":"review-plan-panel.tsx","file":"review-plan-panel.tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"},{"type":"text","value":" does not run in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call that paused. It\nruns once at the start of the next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call, after the client answers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"setup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":" on that second request. Each\ngeneric resume item includes the original request in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":". If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis present and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is missing, the server throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.for(definition)"},{"type":"text","value":" for one typed definition. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.all()"},{"type":"text","value":" for every registered definition. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.all(definitionA, definitionB)"},{"type":"text","value":" to read a typed subset."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook can return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolResume: 'continue'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'cancel'"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'stop'"},{"type":"text","value":". Results\nfrom all middleware combine by the most restrictive rule: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":" wins over\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"},{"type":"text","value":" wins over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook cannot change prompts, tools, or messages. Store the answer on a\ncapability, then return those fields from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase === 'beforeModel'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Can change"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptBoundary"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nothing. It can only pause."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pending-tool policy ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolResume"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full resume order, plus an example that writes a user note into the\nsystem prompt, is in "},{"type":"link","href":"../interrupts/apply-answers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply Answers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onbeforetoolcall","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onBeforeToolCall"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called before each tool executes. The first middleware that returns a non-void decision short-circuits — remaining middleware are skipped for that tool call."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction isRecord(v: unknown): v is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof v === \"object\" && v !== null;\n}\n\nconst guard: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"guard\",\n  onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n    // Block dangerous tools\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"deleteDatabase\") {\n      return { type: \"abort\", reason: \"Dangerous operation blocked\" };\n    }\n\n    // Validate and transform arguments\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"search\" && isRecord(hookCtx.args) && !hookCtx.args.limit) {\n      return {\n        type: \"transformArgs\",\n        args: { ...hookCtx.args, limit: 10 },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decision types:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Continue normally, next middleware can decide"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'transformArgs', args }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace tool arguments before execution"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'skip', result }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skip execution entirely, use provided result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'abort', reason? }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort the entire chat run"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hookCtx"},{"type":"text","value":" provides:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raw tool call object"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tool | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved tool definition"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parsed arguments"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolName"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool call ID"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onaftertoolcall","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onAfterToolCall"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called after each tool execution (or skip). All middleware run — there is no short-circuiting."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolLogger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-logger\",\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    if (info.ok) {\n      console.log(`${info.toolName} completed in ${info.duration}ms`);\n    } else {\n      console.error(`${info.toolName} failed:`, info.error);\n    }\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info"},{"type":"text","value":" object provides:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raw tool call object"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tool | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved tool definition"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolName"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool call ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether execution succeeded"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution time in milliseconds"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result (when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok"},{"type":"text","value":" is true)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error (when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok"},{"type":"text","value":" is false)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tool-hook-order-in-one-turn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool hook order in one turn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the model calls several server tools in one turn, the tools run at the same time:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" runs for each call in call order, before any tool starts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" runs for each tool when it finishes, so in finish order."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A call that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" skips gets its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" right away, before the tools start."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the run aborts before the tools start, no tool runs. Each call gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok: false"},{"type":"text","value":" and the error \"Operation aborted\"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" aborts or throws for a call, the calls before it still run. The error is thrown after they finish."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolExecution: 'sequential'"},{"type":"text","value":", each call finishes its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":", its run, and its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" before the next call starts. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run tools one at a time"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onusage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onUsage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called once per model iteration when the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk includes usage data. Receives the usage object directly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst usageTracker: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"usage-tracker\",\n  onUsage: (ctx, usage) => {\n    console.log(\n      `Iteration ${ctx.iteration}: ${usage.totalTokens} tokens`\n    );\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"promptTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input tokens"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completionTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output tokens"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"totalTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Total tokens"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"terminal-hooks-onfinish-onabort-onerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Terminal Hooks: onFinish, onAbort, onError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exactly "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"one"}]},{"type":"text","value":" terminal hook fires per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" invocation. They are mutually exclusive:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When it fires"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run completed normally"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run was aborted (via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.abort()"},{"type":"text","value":", an external "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":", or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'abort' }"},{"type":"text","value":" decision from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An unhandled error occurred"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" also fires when the invocation pauses at a client-tool or approval wait. The run is not complete yet. To tell a pause from a completion, look in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" for a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outcome.type === 'interrupt'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Separate-finalization path:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Adapters without native-combined support make a separate structured-output provider call after the agent loop."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" fires before the separate provider call, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'structuredOutput'"},{"type":"text","value":" for its chunks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onIteration"},{"type":"text","value":" does "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" fire for finalization; it only fires for agent-loop iterations."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" fires after finalization completes. Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info"},{"type":"text","value":" object reflects the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"agent loop's"}]},{"type":"text","value":" terminal state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.content"},{"type":"text","value":" — the agent loop's accumulated text. Separate-finalization JSON deltas are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" included. Middleware can observe the completed result through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM event in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.usage"},{"type":"text","value":" — the agent loop's last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED.usage"},{"type":"text","value":". For a tools-less structured-output run (no agent-loop iteration produces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":"), this is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":". To capture finalization tokens, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" — that hook fires for "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"every"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" carrying usage, including the finalization call."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":" — the agent loop's last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" when no agent-loop iteration produced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. a tools-less structured-output run)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.duration"},{"type":"text","value":" — wall-clock duration of the entire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" invocation, including finalization."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native-combined output:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Adapters with native-combined support produce the schema-constrained JSON in the regular agent-loop stream. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" does not fire, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" remains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'modelStream'"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onIteration"},{"type":"text","value":" fires for the iteration that produces the JSON. The JSON is agent-loop text, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.content"},{"type":"text","value":" includes it. Middleware observes the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" event in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" during the same phase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On successful completion in either path, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" receives the complete canonical transcript in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.messages"},{"type":"text","value":". Native-combined output keeps the structured result on its terminal assistant message. The separate-finalization path can preserve the agent loop's plain-text assistant message followed by a distinct structured-output assistant message. This transcript is separate from the path-specific fields on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To aggregate usage across the whole run, accumulate from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks rather than relying on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.usage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst terminal: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"terminal\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Finished: ${info.finishReason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n    console.log(`Content: ${info.content}`);\n    if (info.usage) {\n      console.log(`Tokens: ${info.usage.totalTokens}`);\n    }\n  },\n  onAbort: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Aborted: ${info.reason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.error(`Error after ${info.duration}ms:`, info.error);\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info"},{"type":"text","value":" object for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FinishInfo"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent loop's last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" when no agent-loop iteration produced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. a tools-less "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ outputSchema })"},{"type":"text","value":" run)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Total run duration in milliseconds, including any structured-output finalization."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent loop's accumulated text content. Includes native-combined structured JSON; excludes separate-finalization JSON. Observe the completed result through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM event via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ promptTokens; completionTokens; totalTokens } | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The agent loop's last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED.usage"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Does not include finalization tokens"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" to observe those. Always guard with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"if (info.usage)"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.usage?."},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"context-object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Context Object"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every hook receives a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":" as its first argument. It provides request-scoped information and control functions:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unique ID for this chat request"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unique ID for this stream"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI thread identifier. Resolves to caller-provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" (or legacy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conversationId"},{"type":"text","value":"), or an auto-generated value if neither is supplied. Use this for event correlation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conversationId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}]},{"type":"text","value":" alias of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":". Always equals "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"; retained so middleware written before the AG-UI rename keeps working. New middleware should read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewarePhase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current lifecycle phase"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent loop iteration (0-indexed)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunkIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running count of chunks yielded"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External abort signal"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abort(reason?)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort the run from within middleware"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent(name, value, options?)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Push a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk onto the chat stream now. The engine yields it while the current hook is still running, including during "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":". Durability flushes it immediately. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ batch: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep it in the durability batch."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User-provided runtime context value"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defer(promise)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register a non-blocking side-effect"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-runtime-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed Runtime Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a context generic. This lets reusable middleware declared outside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" access the same typed runtime context as your tools."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { session, audit } from \"./server\";\n\ntype AppContext = {\n  userId: string;\n  audit: {\n    write(event: { userId: string; requestId: string }): Promise<void>;\n  };\n};\n\nexport const auditMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<AppContext> = {\n  name: \"audit\",\n  onStart(ctx) {\n    ctx.defer(\n      ctx.context.audit.write({\n        userId: ctx.context.userId,\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [auditMiddleware],\n  context: {\n    userId: session.user.id,\n    audit,\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When typed middleware or typed tools are present, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" checks that the provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" matches the required shape. Existing middleware typed as plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" still works; its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context"},{"type":"text","value":" remains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":" and does not force a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime context is process-local application state. It is separate from AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunAgentInput.context"},{"type":"text","value":", which is protocol metadata parsed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"./runtime-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Context"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for server, client, and client-to-server handoff patterns."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aborting-from-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aborting from Middleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.abort()"},{"type":"text","value":" to gracefully stop the run. This triggers the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" terminal hook:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timeout: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timeout\",\n  onChunk: (ctx) => {\n    if (ctx.chunkIndex > 1000) {\n      ctx.abort(\"Too many chunks\");\n    }\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"deferred-side-effects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred Side Effects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.defer()"},{"type":"text","value":" to register promises that run after the terminal hook without blocking the stream:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst analytics: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"analytics\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      fetch(\"/api/analytics\", {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          requestId: ctx.requestId,\n          duration: info.duration,\n          tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        }),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"composing-multiple-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composing Multiple Middleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware execute in array order. The ordering matters for hooks that pipe or short-circuit:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware } from \"./middleware\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"composition-rules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composition Rules"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Effect of Order"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Piped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — each receives previous output"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier middleware transforms first"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Piped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — each receives previous output"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier middleware transforms first"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequential"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All run in order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Piped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — chunks flow through each middleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If first drops a chunk, later middleware never see it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First-win"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — first non-void decision wins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier middleware has priority"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onShouldContinue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AND"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — any explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" stops the loop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Order only affects which middleware runs first when short-circuiting"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAfterToolCall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequential"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All run in order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequential"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All run in order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish/onAbort/onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequential"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All run in order"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"capabilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware often need to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"share state"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A provider middleware sets something up (a database handle, a per-request counter, a sandbox), and a consumer middleware reads it back later in the same run. Capabilities make that hand-off "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type-safe and order-checked"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the consumer declares what it needs, the provider declares what it offers, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" refuses to run (at compile time "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime) if a required capability was never provided."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creating-a-capability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creating a capability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A capability is created with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCapability<TValue>()('name')"},{"type":"text","value":" — a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"curried"}]},{"type":"text","value":" call:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCapability } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The currying is deliberate: you supply the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value type"}]},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<{ value: number }>"},{"type":"text","value":") while the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name literal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is inferred from the argument ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"counter\""},{"type":"text","value":"). A single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCapability<T>('name')"},{"type":"text","value":" call can't do both — supplying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly stops TypeScript inferring the name, collapsing it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" and defeating the compile-time coverage check that keys on the literal name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"counterCapability"},{"type":"text","value":" is a hybrid value:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"destructures to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[get, provide]"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the two accessors you use inside hooks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"is itself the identity"}]},{"type":"text","value":" you list in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"},{"type":"text","value":". There is no separate token to import."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The accessors:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCounter(ctx)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the value. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if the capability was never provided."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCounter(ctx, { optional: true })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue | undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" — no throw when absent."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provideCounter(ctx, value)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets the value for this run. Call it from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalently, the context exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.get(capability)"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.getOptional(capability)"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.provide(capability, value)"},{"type":"text","value":" — pass the capability handle directly. These are typed by the handle you pass ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.get(counterCapability)"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the value type), so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCounter(ctx)"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.get(counterCapability)"},{"type":"text","value":" are interchangeable — use whichever reads better in your hook."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capability names must be unique across your app."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference), so two capabilities sharing a name will conflate in the type-level check."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-setup-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisioning happens in a dedicated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup(ctx)"},{"type":"text","value":" hook. It "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runs first"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — before any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" (init), across all middleware in array order — so that by the time the rest of the lifecycle begins, every capability is in place. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" receives the stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":" (not the mutable config), and may be async."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"requires-provides-optionalrequires","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"optionalRequires"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three array fields on a middleware declare its capability contract. Each is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReadonlyArray<CapabilityHandle>"},{"type":"text","value":" — you list the capability handles themselves:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities this middleware sets up. Each one "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"must"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provide"},{"type":"text","value":"d inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws after the setup phase."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities this middleware reads. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates (compile time + runtime) that some earlier middleware provides each one."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"optionalRequires"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities used "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"if present"}]},{"type":"text","value":" but not required. Non-gating — never causes a validation error. Read with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getX(ctx, { optional: true })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"array-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author middleware with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChatMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" — it sharpens the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple types so the coverage check and builder can read them precisely. Here a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" sets up a counter in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":", and a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"consumer"}]},{"type":"text","value":" reads it in a hook:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\n// Provider: declares `provides` and provisions the value in `setup`.\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\n// Consumer: declares `requires` and reads the value via `get` in a hook.\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n  onFinish(ctx) {\n    console.log(`Saw ${getCounter(ctx).value} chunks`);\n  },\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  // Provider must come before the consumer.\n  middleware: [withCounter, countsChunks],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you drop "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withCounter"},{"type":"text","value":" from the array, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" reports a compile-time error at the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" option naming the missing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"counter\""},{"type":"text","value":" capability — and throws at runtime before the adapter is ever called."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"builder-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builder example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatMiddleware()"},{"type":"text","value":" builds the array through chained "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls and enforces "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider-before-consumer ordering at compile time"}]},{"type":"text","value":": each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use()"},{"type":"text","value":" requires that the middleware's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" are already covered by capabilities provided by earlier "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n});\n\nconst middleware = createChatMiddleware()\n  .use(withCounter) // provides \"counter\"\n  .use(countsChunks) // requires \"counter\" — OK, already provided above\n  .build();\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Swap the two "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use(countsChunks).use(withCounter)"},{"type":"text","value":") and the builder rejects it at the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".use(countsChunks)"},{"type":"text","value":" line — the consumer is ordered before its provider, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"counter\""},{"type":"text","value":" isn't in the provided set yet."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"validation-guarantees","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation guarantees"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The capability system fails loudly and early:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compile-time coverage."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A required capability that nothing provides surfaces as a type error at the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" option. This is enforced two ways: an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array coverage check"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware: [...]"},{"type":"text","value":", and the order-aware "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatMiddleware()"},{"type":"text","value":" builder"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (which additionally enforces ordering)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime coverage."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Even if types are bypassed, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates coverage and "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throws before the adapter runs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if a required capability is missing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Post-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" assertion."}]},{"type":"text","value":" If a middleware declares a capability in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"},{"type":"text","value":" but never calls its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provide"},{"type":"text","value":" accessor during "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws after the setup phase — you can't silently forget to provision."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Duplicate provide → last-wins + warning."}]},{"type":"text","value":" If two middleware provide the same capability, the last write wins and a development warning is emitted."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unique names."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Capability "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":"s must be unique across your app; the compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"built-in-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Middleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI ships ready-made middleware for common cases — caching tool results, redacting streamed text, and OpenTelemetry tracing:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCacheMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache tool-call results by name + arguments"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentGuardMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redact / transform / block streamed text content"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./built-in-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full options and examples for each. The recipes below show how to build your own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"recipes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recipes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"live-custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live custom events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A long "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" hook can send progress to the client while it waits. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" when the work starts, then again when it finishes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:started\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:ended\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine yields each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk as soon as you call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":". If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" is not on the wire yet, the engine sends it first. Durability then flushes the event so the client can render a live indicator. Read these events on the client the same way as tool "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" calls. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../protocol/custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rate-limiting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate Limiting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limit the number of tool calls per request:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(maxCalls: number): ChatMiddleware {\n  let toolCallCount = 0;\n  return {\n    name: \"rate-limit\",\n    onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n      toolCallCount++;\n      if (toolCallCount > maxCalls) {\n        return {\n          type: \"abort\",\n          reason: `Rate limit: exceeded ${maxCalls} tool calls`,\n        };\n      }\n    },\n  };\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"audit-trail","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audit Trail"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Log every action for compliance:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditTrail: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"audit-trail\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_started\",\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"tool_executed\",\n        toolName: info.toolName,\n        success: info.ok,\n        duration: info.duration,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_finished\",\n        duration: info.duration,\n        tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"per-iteration-tool-swapping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-Iteration Tool Swapping"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose different tools at different stages of the agent loop:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolSwapper: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-swapper\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n\n    if (ctx.iteration === 0) {\n      // First iteration: only allow search\n      return {\n        tools: config.tools.filter((t) => t.name === \"search\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Later iterations: allow all tools\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"content-filtering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Content Filtering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drop or transform chunks before they reach the consumer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { containsProfanity } from \"./filters\";\n\nconst contentFilter: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"content-filter\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      if (containsProfanity(chunk.delta)) {\n        // Drop the chunk entirely\n        return null;\n      }\n    }\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error-recovery-with-retry-logging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Recovery with Retry Logging"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { alertService } from \"./services\";\n\nconst errorRecovery: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"error-recovery\",\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      alertService.send({\n        level: \"error\",\n        message: `Chat ${ctx.requestId} failed after ${info.duration}ms`,\n        error: String(info.error),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typescript-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The core middleware types are exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  ChatMiddleware,\n  ChatMiddlewareContext,\n  ChatMiddlewarePhase,\n  ChatMiddlewareConfig,\n  StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig,\n  ToolCallHookContext,\n  BeforeToolCallDecision,\n  AfterToolCallInfo,\n  IterationInfo,\n  ToolPhaseCompleteInfo,\n  UsageInfo,\n  FinishInfo,\n  AbortInfo,\n  ErrorInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The option/type surfaces for the "},{"type":"link","href":"./built-in-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are exported from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath (not the main barrel):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  ToolCacheMiddlewareOptions,\n  ToolCacheStorage,\n  ToolCacheEntry,\n  ContentGuardMiddlewareOptions,\n  ContentGuardRule,\n  ContentFilteredInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./built-in-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCacheMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentGuardMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./compaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":": keep long chats under the context limit with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withCompaction"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./otel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenTelemetry"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — emit traces and metrics via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":"- "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Learn about the isomorphic tool system"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/agentic-cycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agentic Cycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Understand the multi-step agent loop"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — How streaming works in TanStack AI"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"lifecycle-overview","text":"Lifecycle Overview","level":2},{"id":"phase-transitions","text":"Phase Transitions","level":3},{"id":"hooks-reference","text":"Hooks Reference","level":2},{"id":"onconfig","text":"onConfig","level":3},{"id":"onstructuredoutputconfig","text":"onStructuredOutputConfig","level":3},{"id":"onstart","text":"onStart","level":3},{"id":"onchunk","text":"onChunk","level":3},{"id":"chunk-types-you-ll-see","text":"Chunk types you'll see","level":4},{"id":"transforming-structured-output-chunks","text":"Transforming structured-output chunks","level":4},{"id":"onshouldcontinue","text":"onShouldContinue","level":3},{"id":"oninterruptboundary-and-oninterruptresolution","text":"onInterruptBoundary and onInterruptResolution","level":3},{"id":"onbeforetoolcall","text":"onBeforeToolCall","level":3},{"id":"onaftertoolcall","text":"onAfterToolCall","level":3},{"id":"tool-hook-order-in-one-turn","text":"Tool hook order in one turn","level":3},{"id":"onusage","text":"onUsage","level":3},{"id":"terminal-hooks-onfinish-onabort-onerror","text":"Terminal Hooks: onFinish, onAbort, onError","level":3},{"id":"context-object","text":"Context Object","level":2},{"id":"typed-runtime-context","text":"Typed Runtime Context","level":2},{"id":"aborting-from-middleware","text":"Aborting from Middleware","level":3},{"id":"deferred-side-effects","text":"Deferred Side Effects","level":3},{"id":"composing-multiple-middleware","text":"Composing Multiple Middleware","level":2},{"id":"composition-rules","text":"Composition Rules","level":3},{"id":"capabilities","text":"Capabilities","level":2},{"id":"creating-a-capability","text":"Creating a capability","level":3},{"id":"the-setup-hook","text":"The setup hook","level":3},{"id":"requires-provides-optionalrequires","text":"requires / provides / optionalRequires","level":3},{"id":"array-example","text":"Array example","level":3},{"id":"builder-example","text":"Builder example","level":3},{"id":"validation-guarantees","text":"Validation guarantees","level":3},{"id":"built-in-middleware","text":"Built-in Middleware","level":2},{"id":"recipes","text":"Recipes","level":2},{"id":"live-custom-events","text":"Live custom events","level":3},{"id":"rate-limiting","text":"Rate Limiting","level":3},{"id":"audit-trail","text":"Audit Trail","level":3},{"id":"per-iteration-tool-swapping","text":"Per-Iteration Tool Swapping","level":3},{"id":"content-filtering","text":"Content Filtering","level":3},{"id":"error-recovery-with-retry-logging","text":"Error Recovery with Retry Logging","level":3},{"id":"typescript-types","text":"TypeScript Types","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nMiddleware lets you hook into every stage of the `chat()` lifecycle — from configuration to streaming, tool execution, usage tracking, and completion. You can observe, transform, or short-circuit behavior at each stage without modifying your adapter or tool implementations.\n\nCommon use cases include:\n\n- **Logging and observability** — track token usage, tool execution timing, errors\n- **Configuration transforms** — inject system prompts, adjust temperature per iteration, filter tools\n- **Stream processing** — redact sensitive content, transform chunks, drop unwanted events\n- **Tool call interception** — validate arguments, cache results, abort on dangerous calls\n- **Side effects** — send analytics, update databases, trigger notifications\n\n## Quick Start\n\nPass an array of middleware to the `chat()` function:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst logger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"logger\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Chat started`);\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Finished in ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [logger],\n});\n```\n\n> **Just want to see chunks flowing through your middleware during development?**\n> Use `debug: { middleware: true }` on your `chat()` call — no custom middleware required. See [Debug Logging](./debug-logging).\n\n## Lifecycle Overview\n\nEvery `chat()` invocation follows a predictable lifecycle. Middleware hooks fire at specific phases:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"chat() called\"] --> B[\"onConfig (phase: init)\"]\n    B --> C[onStart]\n    C --> D[\"onConfig (phase: beforeModel)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Adapter streams response\"]\n    E --> F[\"onChunk (for each chunk)\"]\n    F --> G{Tool calls?}\n    G -->|No| H[onUsage]\n    G -->|Yes| I[onBeforeToolCall]\n    I --> J[Tool executes]\n    J --> K[onAfterToolCall]\n    K --> L{Continue loop?}\n    L -->|Yes| D\n    L -->|No| H\n    H --> SO{\"Structured output path?\"}\n    SO -->|None| M{Outcome}\n    SO -->|\"Native combined\"| SOH[\"Post-loop structured-output harvest (onChunk)\"]\n    SOH --> M\n    SO -->|\"Separate finalization\"| SOC[onStructuredOutputConfig]\n    SOC --> SOM[\"onConfig (phase: structuredOutput)\"]\n    SOM --> SOS[\"Structured-output finalization (onChunk, onUsage)\"]\n    SOS --> M\n    M -->|Success| N[onFinish]\n    M -->|Abort| O[onAbort]\n    M -->|Error| P[onError]\n\n    style I fill:#e1f5ff\n    style J fill:#ffe1e1\n    style SOC fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOM fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOS fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOH fill:#e1f5ff\n    style N fill:#e1ffe1\n    style O fill:#fff4e1\n    style P fill:#ffe1e1\n```\n\n### Phase Transitions\n\nThe context's `phase` field tracks where you are in the lifecycle:\n\n| Phase | When | Hooks Called |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `init` | Once at startup | `onConfig` |\n| `beforeModel` | Before each model call (per iteration) | `onConfig` |\n| `modelStream` | While adapter streams chunks | `onChunk`, `onUsage` |\n| `beforeTools` | Before tool execution | `onBeforeToolCall` |\n| `afterTools` | After tool execution | `onAfterToolCall` |\n| `structuredOutput` | During the final structured-output adapter call (when `outputSchema` is set **and** `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options). Chunks from `adapter.structuredOutputStream` (or the synthesized non-streaming fallback) flow through `onChunk` with this phase, and `onUsage` fires for the final call's tokens. **Does not fire** for adapters that natively combine tools + schema in one streaming call (modern OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x family, and OpenRouter when every routed model is in `OPENROUTER_COMBINED_TOOLS_AND_SCHEMA_MODELS`; see issue #605). On that path middleware observes the run through `beforeModel` / `modelStream` as usual. | `onStructuredOutputConfig`, `onConfig`, `onChunk`, `onUsage` |\n\n## Hooks Reference\n\n### onConfig\n\nCalled once during `init` (startup) and once per iteration during `beforeModel` (before each model call). On the separate-finalization path, `onConfig` additionally re-fires at the structured-output boundary with `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'`, receiving the post-`onStructuredOutputConfig` view of the config. A single-iteration separate-finalization run therefore fires `onConfig` three times (`init` + `beforeModel` + `structuredOutput`). Native-combined output does not add this third call. Use `onConfig` to transform the configuration that the model receives.\n\nReturn a **partial** config object with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config automatically. No need to spread the existing config.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst dynamicTemperature: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"dynamic-temperature\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase === \"init\") {\n      // Add a system prompt at startup — only systemPrompts is overwritten\n      return {\n        systemPrompts: [\n          ...config.systemPrompts,\n          \"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n        ],\n      };\n    }\n\n    if (ctx.phase === \"beforeModel\" && ctx.iteration > 0) {\n      // Increase temperature on retries. Sampling params live in the\n      // provider-native modelOptions object — `temperature` is universal,\n      // so it's the same key across providers. Spread the existing\n      // modelOptions so other model options stay unchanged.\n      const current =\n        typeof config.modelOptions?.temperature === \"number\"\n          ? config.modelOptions.temperature\n          : 0.7;\n      return {\n        modelOptions: {\n          ...config.modelOptions,\n          temperature: Math.min(current + 0.1, 1.0),\n        },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n> Sampling parameters (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the various `max*Tokens` keys) live inside `modelOptions` under each provider's native name — they are no longer root config fields. `temperature` happens to be spelled the same across every provider, so the example above is provider-agnostic; if you mutate a token limit instead, use the provider-native key (e.g. `max_output_tokens` for OpenAI, `num_predict` nested under `modelOptions.options` for Ollama). See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n**Config fields you can transform:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `messages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Canonical conversation history. Persistence and `ctx.messages` use this field. |\n| `providerMessages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Temporary context sent to the provider. Defaults to `messages`. |\n| `systemPrompts` | `string[]` | System prompts |\n| `tools` | `Tool[]` | Available tools |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Request metadata |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Provider-native options — this is where sampling params (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the provider's `max*Tokens` key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options). |\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onConfig`, the config is **piped** through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware.\n\nReturn `providerMessages` when a transform must affect only the model call. For\ncompatibility, returning `messages` also updates provider input unless the same\nresult sets `providerMessages` explicitly.\n\n### onStructuredOutputConfig\n\nCalled once at the start of the final structured-output adapter call — only when `chat()` was invoked with `outputSchema` **and** `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options. Pipes through middleware in order, like `onConfig`, but with access to the **JSON Schema** being sent to the provider. Use this hook when you need to transform the schema (e.g., inject `$defs`, strip vendor-incompatible keywords) or apply structured-output-specific behavior (e.g., suppress system prompts on the final call).\n\n> Native-combined adapters (modern OpenAI, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605) skip the separate finalization call and never invoke this hook. The engine passes the converted schema directly to `chatStream` after `onConfig` runs, so middleware cannot transform the native-combined schema.\n\nReturn a **partial** `StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig` with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config. Return `void` to pass through.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { sharedDefs } from \"./defs\";\n\nconst injectDefs: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"inject-defs\",\n  onStructuredOutputConfig: (_ctx, config) => {\n    // `config.outputSchema` is the JSON Schema being sent to the provider\n    return {\n      outputSchema: {\n        ...config.outputSchema,\n        $defs: { ...sharedDefs },\n      },\n    };\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Config fields you can transform:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `messages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Canonical conversation history |\n| `providerMessages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Temporary context sent to the final call |\n| `systemPrompts` | `SystemPrompt[]` | System prompts on the final call |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Request metadata |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Provider-native options — this is where sampling params (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the provider's `max*Tokens` key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options). |\n| `outputSchema` | `JSONSchema` | JSON Schema being sent to the provider for structured output |\n\n**Ordering at the structured-output boundary:**\n\n1. `onStructuredOutputConfig` fires first, piping through every middleware in array order.\n2. `onConfig` then re-fires at the same boundary with `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'`, receiving the post-`onStructuredOutputConfig` view of the config (minus `outputSchema`). Use `onConfig` for general-purpose transforms that apply to every adapter call; use `onStructuredOutputConfig` when you need access to the schema.\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onStructuredOutputConfig`, the config is **piped** through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware.\n\n### onStart\n\nCalled once after the initial `onConfig` completes. Use it for setup tasks like initializing timers or logging.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timer: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timer\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`Request ${ctx.requestId} started at iteration ${ctx.iteration}`);\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### onChunk\n\nCalled for every chunk streamed from the adapter. You can observe, transform, expand, or drop chunks.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactor: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redactor\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      // Transform: redact sensitive content\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Return void to pass through unchanged\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Return values:**\n\n| Return | Effect |\n|--------|--------|\n| `void` / `undefined` | Chunk passes through unchanged |\n| `StreamChunk` | Replaces the original chunk |\n| `StreamChunk[]` | Expands into multiple chunks |\n| `null` | Drops the chunk entirely |\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onChunk`, chunks flow through them in order. If one middleware drops a chunk (returns `null`), subsequent middleware never see it.\n\n#### Chunk types you'll see\n\n`onChunk` receives every [AG-UI event](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) the run produces — not just text. Narrow on `chunk.type` (a discriminated union) before reading type-specific fields. The common ones:\n\n| `chunk.type` | Meaning | Key fields |\n|--------------|---------|-----------|\n| `RUN_STARTED` / `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERROR` | Run lifecycle boundaries | `runId`, `finishReason`, `usage` (on finish), `message` (on error) |\n| `TEXT_MESSAGE_START` / `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` / `TEXT_MESSAGE_END` | Assistant text streaming | `messageId`, `delta` (content) |\n| `TOOL_CALL_START` / `TOOL_CALL_ARGS` / `TOOL_CALL_END` | Tool invocation streaming | `toolCallId`, `toolCallName`, `delta` (args), result on end |\n| `STEP_STARTED` / `STEP_FINISHED` | Thinking / reasoning steps | `delta`, `signature` |\n| `STATE_SNAPSHOT` / `STATE_DELTA` | Agent state sync | `snapshot`, `delta` |\n| `CUSTOM` | Extensibility events (incl. structured-output — see below) | `name`, `value` |\n\nSee the [AG-UI protocol docs](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) for the full event catalogue and exact field shapes.\n\n#### Transforming structured-output chunks\n\nThere is **no separate `onStructuredOutputChunk` hook** — and you don't need one. When `chat()` is invoked with `outputSchema`, the structured-output chunks (the JSON `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` deltas, plus the `structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM events and any finalization `RUN_ERROR`) flow through the **same `onChunk` hook** as everything else. You transform, expand, or drop them exactly like any other chunk.\n\nHow you distinguish them depends on which finalization path the adapter takes:\n\n- **Separate-finalization adapters** (`supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options): `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'` during the finalization call. Discriminate on the phase.\n- **Native-combined adapters** (modern OpenAI Chat Completions / Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605): the schema-constrained JSON is produced on the model's natural final turn, so **`ctx.phase` stays `'modelStream'`** — the `'structuredOutput'` phase never fires. Discriminate on the CUSTOM event name (`structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete`) instead.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactStructuredOutput: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redact-structured-output\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    // Separate-finalization path: the JSON streams as TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\n    // during the 'structuredOutput' phase. Transform the delta like any\n    // other text chunk — here, redact anything that looks like an SSN before\n    // it reaches the client.\n    if (\n      ctx.phase === \"structuredOutput\" &&\n      chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"\n    ) {\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n\n    // Both paths: the completed typed payload arrives as a CUSTOM\n    // `structured-output.complete` event. On the native-combined path this is\n    // your only signal (ctx.phase never flips to 'structuredOutput'), so key\n    // off the event name, not the phase. `chunk.value` carries { object, raw }.\n    if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n      console.log(\"final structured output:\", chunk.value);\n    }\n\n    // Return void to pass everything else through unchanged.\n  },\n};\n```\n\n> Why is there `onStructuredOutputConfig` but no `onStructuredOutputChunk`? Because the **config** shape genuinely differs at the structured-output boundary — it carries an `outputSchema` field that plain `ChatMiddlewareConfig` doesn't (see [onStructuredOutputConfig](#onstructuredoutputconfig)). **Chunks** are all just `StreamChunk` regardless of phase, so one `onChunk` plus `ctx.phase` (or the CUSTOM event name) covers every case — a parallel chunk hook would be redundant.\n\n### onShouldContinue\n\nCalled when the engine is deciding whether to start another agent-loop iteration (after a tool phase or between model turns). Combined with AND semantics across middleware **and** with `agentLoopStrategy` — any explicit `false` stops the loop. Return `true`, `void`, or `undefined` to allow continuation.\n\nDoes **not** abort the run: the stream finishes normally with the current messages. Use `ctx.abort()` only for a hard abort.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst budget: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-budget\",\n  onShouldContinue: (_ctx, state) => {\n    // Stop further turns once 20 tool calls have been emitted\n    if (state.toolCallCount >= 20) return false;\n  },\n};\n```\n\nFor a full per-turn + cumulative tool budget recipe, see [Tool-call budgets](../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe).\n\n### onInterruptBoundary and onInterruptResolution\n\nUse these hooks when middleware needs data from the client. Define the request\nwith `defineInterrupt()` and register it with `chat({ interrupts })` and\n`useChat({ interrupts })`. Do not emit raw AG-UI events from middleware.\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` runs at four points in an agent iteration:\n\n- `beforeModel`, before the adapter starts.\n- `afterModel`, after the model response is complete.\n- `beforeTools`, before tool execution starts.\n- `afterTools`, after the tool phase is complete.\n\nEach middleware can return requests from one boundary. The engine combines all\nrequests from that boundary into one AG-UI interrupt batch. The batch ends the\nrun with one interrupt outcome.\n\nThis hook cannot change config. Its only legal return is `{ interrupts }` or\nnothing. The continuation is a new `chat()` call, so the hook runs again. Skip\nthe emit when `ctx.parentRunId` is set if this pause belongs to the original\nrequest only.\n\nWhat is in `ctx` at each phase, and when to use each phase, is in\n[Lifecycle Boundaries](../interrupts/boundaries).\n\nCreate one shared definition. Both the server and the client import this value,\nso the definition ID and response shape stay the same on both sides.\n\n```typescript title=\"review-plan.ts\"\nimport { defineInterrupt, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const reviewPlan = defineInterrupt({\n  id: 'review-plan',\n  payloadSchema: z.object({ title: z.string() }),\n  responseSchema: z.object({ approved: z.boolean() }),\n})\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeTools') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'release-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Approve this plan?',\n          payload: { title: 'Release plan' },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nRegister the definition on the server. Forward `parentRunId` and `resume` so\na client resolution starts the continuation with its full context.\n\n```typescript title=\"route.ts\"\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequestBody,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware, reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequestBody(await request.json())\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nRegister the same definition on the client. Check `kind` and `definitionId`.\nTypeScript then treats the item as `GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>`.\n`resolveInterrupt` uses the response shape from `reviewPlan.responseSchema`.\n\n```tsx title=\"review-plan-panel.tsx\"\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { GenericInterrupt } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nfunction ReviewCard({\n  interrupt,\n}: {\n  interrupt: GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>\n}) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt({ approved: true })}\n    >\n      Approve plan\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n\nexport function ReviewPlanPanel() {\n  const { interrupts, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button onClick={() => sendMessage('Review the release plan')}>\n        Start review\n      </button>\n      {interrupts.map((interrupt) => {\n        if (interrupt.kind !== 'generic') return null\n        if (!('definitionId' in interrupt)) return null\n        if (interrupt.definitionId !== reviewPlan.id) return null\n        return <ReviewCard key={interrupt.id} interrupt={interrupt} />\n      })}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`onInterruptResolution` does not run in the `chat()` call that paused. It\nruns once at the start of the next `chat()` call, after the client answers.\n\n```\nsetup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop\n```\n\n`useChat` sends `parentRunId` and `resume` on that second request. Each\ngeneric resume item includes the original request in `metadata`. If `resume`\nis present and `parentRunId` is missing, the server throws.\n\nUse `resumedInterrupts.for(definition)` for one typed definition. Use\n`resumedInterrupts.all()` for every registered definition. Use\n`resumedInterrupts.all(definitionA, definitionB)` to read a typed subset.\n\nThe hook can return `toolResume: 'continue'`, `'cancel'`, or `'stop'`. Results\nfrom all middleware combine by the most restrictive rule: `stop` wins over\n`cancel`, and `cancel` wins over `continue`.\n\nThis hook cannot change prompts, tools, or messages. Store the answer on a\ncapability, then return those fields from `onConfig` when\n`ctx.phase === 'beforeModel'`.\n\n| Hook | Can change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `onInterruptBoundary` | Nothing. It can only pause. |\n| `onInterruptResolution` | Pending-tool policy (`toolResume`) |\n| `onConfig` | `messages`, `systemPrompts`, `tools`, `modelOptions`, `metadata` |\n\nThe full resume order, plus an example that writes a user note into the\nsystem prompt, is in [Apply Answers](../interrupts/apply-answers).\n\n### onBeforeToolCall\n\nCalled before each tool executes. The first middleware that returns a non-void decision short-circuits — remaining middleware are skipped for that tool call.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction isRecord(v: unknown): v is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof v === \"object\" && v !== null;\n}\n\nconst guard: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"guard\",\n  onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n    // Block dangerous tools\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"deleteDatabase\") {\n      return { type: \"abort\", reason: \"Dangerous operation blocked\" };\n    }\n\n    // Validate and transform arguments\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"search\" && isRecord(hookCtx.args) && !hookCtx.args.limit) {\n      return {\n        type: \"transformArgs\",\n        args: { ...hookCtx.args, limit: 10 },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Decision types:**\n\n| Decision | Effect |\n|----------|--------|\n| `void` / `undefined` | Continue normally, next middleware can decide |\n| `{ type: 'transformArgs', args }` | Replace tool arguments before execution |\n| `{ type: 'skip', result }` | Skip execution entirely, use provided result |\n| `{ type: 'abort', reason? }` | Abort the entire chat run |\n\nThe `hookCtx` provides:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `toolCall` | `ToolCall` | Raw tool call object |\n| `tool` | `Tool \\| undefined` | Resolved tool definition |\n| `args` | `unknown` | Parsed arguments |\n| `toolName` | `string` | Tool name |\n| `toolCallId` | `string` | Tool call ID |\n\n### onAfterToolCall\n\nCalled after each tool execution (or skip). All middleware run — there is no short-circuiting.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolLogger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-logger\",\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    if (info.ok) {\n      console.log(`${info.toolName} completed in ${info.duration}ms`);\n    } else {\n      console.error(`${info.toolName} failed:`, info.error);\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `info` object provides:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `toolCall` | `ToolCall` | Raw tool call object |\n| `tool` | `Tool \\| undefined` | Resolved tool definition |\n| `toolName` | `string` | Tool name |\n| `toolCallId` | `string` | Tool call ID |\n| `ok` | `boolean` | Whether execution succeeded |\n| `duration` | `number` | Execution time in milliseconds |\n| `result` | `unknown` | Result (when `ok` is true) |\n| `error` | `unknown` | Error (when `ok` is false) |\n\n### Tool hook order in one turn\n\nWhen the model calls several server tools in one turn, the tools run at the same time:\n\n- `onBeforeToolCall` runs for each call in call order, before any tool starts.\n- `onAfterToolCall` runs for each tool when it finishes, so in finish order.\n- A call that `onBeforeToolCall` skips gets its `onAfterToolCall` right away, before the tools start.\n- If the run aborts before the tools start, no tool runs. Each call gets `onAfterToolCall` with `ok: false` and the error \"Operation aborted\".\n- If `onBeforeToolCall` aborts or throws for a call, the calls before it still run. The error is thrown after they finish.\n\nWith `toolExecution: 'sequential'`, each call finishes its `onBeforeToolCall`, its run, and its `onAfterToolCall` before the next call starts. See [Run tools one at a time](../tools/tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time).\n\n### onUsage\n\nCalled once per model iteration when the `RUN_FINISHED` chunk includes usage data. Receives the usage object directly.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst usageTracker: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"usage-tracker\",\n  onUsage: (ctx, usage) => {\n    console.log(\n      `Iteration ${ctx.iteration}: ${usage.totalTokens} tokens`\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `usage` object:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `promptTokens` | `number` | Input tokens |\n| `completionTokens` | `number` | Output tokens |\n| `totalTokens` | `number` | Total tokens |\n\n### Terminal Hooks: onFinish, onAbort, onError\n\nExactly **one** terminal hook fires per `chat()` invocation. They are mutually exclusive:\n\n| Hook | When it fires |\n|------|--------------|\n| `onFinish` | Run completed normally |\n| `onAbort` | Run was aborted (via `ctx.abort()`, an external `AbortSignal`, or a `{ type: 'abort' }` decision from `onBeforeToolCall`) |\n| `onError` | An unhandled error occurred |\n\n`onFinish` also fires when the invocation pauses at a client-tool or approval wait. The run is not complete yet. To tell a pause from a completion, look in `onChunk` for a `RUN_FINISHED` chunk with `outcome.type === 'interrupt'`.\n\n> **Separate-finalization path:** Adapters without native-combined support make a separate structured-output provider call after the agent loop.\n>\n> - `onStructuredOutputConfig` fires before the separate provider call, and `ctx.phase` is `'structuredOutput'` for its chunks.\n> - `onIteration` does **not** fire for finalization; it only fires for agent-loop iterations.\n> - `onFinish` fires after finalization completes. Its `info` object reflects the **agent loop's** terminal state.\n> - `info.content` — the agent loop's accumulated text. Separate-finalization JSON deltas are **not** included. Middleware can observe the completed result through the `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM event in `onChunk`.\n> - `info.usage` — the agent loop's last `RUN_FINISHED.usage`. For a tools-less structured-output run (no agent-loop iteration produces `RUN_FINISHED`), this is `undefined`. To capture finalization tokens, use `onUsage` — that hook fires for **every** `RUN_FINISHED` carrying usage, including the finalization call.\n> - `info.finishReason` — the agent loop's last `finishReason`. `null` when no agent-loop iteration produced `RUN_FINISHED` (e.g. a tools-less structured-output run).\n> - `info.duration` — wall-clock duration of the entire `chat()` invocation, including finalization.\n>\n> **Native-combined output:** Adapters with native-combined support produce the schema-constrained JSON in the regular agent-loop stream. `onStructuredOutputConfig` does not fire, `ctx.phase` remains `'modelStream'`, and `onIteration` fires for the iteration that produces the JSON. The JSON is agent-loop text, so `info.content` includes it. Middleware observes the `structured-output.complete` event in `onChunk` during the same phase.\n>\n> On successful completion in either path, `onFinish` receives the complete canonical transcript in `ctx.messages`. Native-combined output keeps the structured result on its terminal assistant message. The separate-finalization path can preserve the agent loop's plain-text assistant message followed by a distinct structured-output assistant message. This transcript is separate from the path-specific fields on `info`.\n>\n> To aggregate usage across the whole run, accumulate from `onUsage` callbacks rather than relying on `info.usage`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst terminal: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"terminal\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Finished: ${info.finishReason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n    console.log(`Content: ${info.content}`);\n    if (info.usage) {\n      console.log(`Tokens: ${info.usage.totalTokens}`);\n    }\n  },\n  onAbort: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Aborted: ${info.reason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.error(`Error after ${info.duration}ms:`, info.error);\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `info` object for `onFinish` (`FinishInfo`):\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `finishReason` | `string \\| null` | The agent loop's last `finishReason`. `null` when no agent-loop iteration produced `RUN_FINISHED` (e.g. a tools-less `chat({ outputSchema })` run). |\n| `duration` | `number` | Total run duration in milliseconds, including any structured-output finalization. |\n| `content` | `string` | The agent loop's accumulated text content. Includes native-combined structured JSON; excludes separate-finalization JSON. Observe the completed result through the `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM event via `onChunk`. |\n| `usage` | `{ promptTokens; completionTokens; totalTokens } \\| undefined` | **Optional.** The agent loop's last `RUN_FINISHED.usage`. **Does not include finalization tokens** — use `onUsage` to observe those. Always guard with `if (info.usage)` or `info.usage?.`. |\n\n## Context Object\n\nEvery hook receives a `ChatMiddlewareContext` as its first argument. It provides request-scoped information and control functions:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `requestId` | `string` | Unique ID for this chat request |\n| `streamId` | `string` | Unique ID for this stream |\n| `threadId` | `string` | AG-UI thread identifier. Resolves to caller-provided `threadId` (or legacy `conversationId`), or an auto-generated value if neither is supplied. Use this for event correlation. |\n| `conversationId` | `string \\| undefined` | **Deprecated** alias of `threadId`. Always equals `ctx.threadId`; retained so middleware written before the AG-UI rename keeps working. New middleware should read `ctx.threadId`. |\n| `phase` | `ChatMiddlewarePhase` | Current lifecycle phase |\n| `iteration` | `number` | Agent loop iteration (0-indexed) |\n| `chunkIndex` | `number` | Running count of chunks yielded |\n| `signal` | `AbortSignal \\| undefined` | External abort signal |\n| `abort(reason?)` | `function` | Abort the run from within middleware |\n| `emitCustomEvent(name, value, options?)` | `function` | Push a `CUSTOM` chunk onto the chat stream now. The engine yields it while the current hook is still running, including during `onConfig`. Durability flushes it immediately. Pass `{ batch: true }` to keep it in the durability batch. |\n| `context` | `TContext` | User-provided runtime context value |\n| `defer(promise)` | `function` | Register a non-blocking side-effect |\n\n## Typed Runtime Context\n\n`ChatMiddleware` accepts a context generic. This lets reusable middleware declared outside `chat()` access the same typed runtime context as your tools.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { session, audit } from \"./server\";\n\ntype AppContext = {\n  userId: string;\n  audit: {\n    write(event: { userId: string; requestId: string }): Promise<void>;\n  };\n};\n\nexport const auditMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<AppContext> = {\n  name: \"audit\",\n  onStart(ctx) {\n    ctx.defer(\n      ctx.context.audit.write({\n        userId: ctx.context.userId,\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [auditMiddleware],\n  context: {\n    userId: session.user.id,\n    audit,\n  },\n});\n```\n\nWhen typed middleware or typed tools are present, `chat()` checks that the provided `context` matches the required shape. Existing middleware typed as plain `ChatMiddleware` still works; its `ctx.context` remains `unknown` and does not force a `context` option.\n\nRuntime context is process-local application state. It is separate from AG-UI `RunAgentInput.context`, which is protocol metadata parsed by `chatParamsFromRequest`. See [Runtime Context](./runtime-context) for server, client, and client-to-server handoff patterns.\n\n### Aborting from Middleware\n\nCall `ctx.abort()` to gracefully stop the run. This triggers the `onAbort` terminal hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timeout: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timeout\",\n  onChunk: (ctx) => {\n    if (ctx.chunkIndex > 1000) {\n      ctx.abort(\"Too many chunks\");\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Deferred Side Effects\n\nUse `ctx.defer()` to register promises that run after the terminal hook without blocking the stream:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst analytics: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"analytics\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      fetch(\"/api/analytics\", {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          requestId: ctx.requestId,\n          duration: info.duration,\n          tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        }),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Composing Multiple Middleware\n\nMiddleware execute in array order. The ordering matters for hooks that pipe or short-circuit:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware } from \"./middleware\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware],\n});\n```\n\n### Composition Rules\n\n| Hook | Composition | Effect of Order |\n|------|------------|----------------|\n| `onConfig` | **Piped** — each receives previous output | Earlier middleware transforms first |\n| `onStructuredOutputConfig` | **Piped** — each receives previous output | Earlier middleware transforms first |\n| `onStart` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onChunk` | **Piped** — chunks flow through each middleware | If first drops a chunk, later middleware never see it |\n| `onBeforeToolCall` | **First-win** — first non-void decision wins | Earlier middleware has priority |\n| `onShouldContinue` | **AND** — any explicit `false` stops the loop | Order only affects which middleware runs first when short-circuiting |\n| `onAfterToolCall` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onUsage` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onFinish/onAbort/onError` | Sequential | All run in order |\n\n## Capabilities\n\nMiddleware often need to **share state**. A provider middleware sets something up (a database handle, a per-request counter, a sandbox), and a consumer middleware reads it back later in the same run. Capabilities make that hand-off **type-safe and order-checked**: the consumer declares what it needs, the provider declares what it offers, and `chat()` refuses to run (at compile time _and_ at runtime) if a required capability was never provided.\n\n### Creating a capability\n\nA capability is created with `createCapability<TValue>()('name')` — a **curried** call:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCapability } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n```\n\nThe currying is deliberate: you supply the **value type** explicitly (`<{ value: number }>`) while the **name literal** is inferred from the argument (`\"counter\"`). A single `createCapability<T>('name')` call can't do both — supplying `T` explicitly stops TypeScript inferring the name, collapsing it to `string` and defeating the compile-time coverage check that keys on the literal name.\n\nThe returned `counterCapability` is a hybrid value:\n\n- It **destructures to `[get, provide]`** — the two accessors you use inside hooks.\n- It **is itself the identity** you list in `requires` / `provides`. There is no separate token to import.\n\nThe accessors:\n\n| Accessor | Behavior |\n|----------|----------|\n| `getCounter(ctx)` | Returns the value. **Throws** if the capability was never provided. |\n| `getCounter(ctx, { optional: true })` | Returns `TValue \\| undefined` — no throw when absent. |\n| `provideCounter(ctx, value)` | Sets the value for this run. Call it from `setup`. |\n\nEquivalently, the context exposes `ctx.get(capability)`, `ctx.getOptional(capability)`, and `ctx.provide(capability, value)` — pass the capability handle directly. These are typed by the handle you pass (`ctx.get(counterCapability)` returns the value type), so `getCounter(ctx)` and `ctx.get(counterCapability)` are interchangeable — use whichever reads better in your hook.\n\n> **Capability names must be unique across your app.** The compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference), so two capabilities sharing a name will conflate in the type-level check.\n\n### The `setup` hook\n\nProvisioning happens in a dedicated `setup(ctx)` hook. It **runs first** — before any `onConfig` (init), across all middleware in array order — so that by the time the rest of the lifecycle begins, every capability is in place. `setup` receives the stable `ChatMiddlewareContext` (not the mutable config), and may be async.\n\n### `requires` / `provides` / `optionalRequires`\n\nThree array fields on a middleware declare its capability contract. Each is a `ReadonlyArray<CapabilityHandle>` — you list the capability handles themselves:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `provides` | Capabilities this middleware sets up. Each one **must** be `provide`d inside `setup`, or `chat()` throws after the setup phase. |\n| `requires` | Capabilities this middleware reads. `chat()` validates (compile time + runtime) that some earlier middleware provides each one. |\n| `optionalRequires` | Capabilities used **if present** but not required. Non-gating — never causes a validation error. Read with `getX(ctx, { optional: true })`. |\n\n### Array example\n\nAuthor middleware with `defineChatMiddleware` — it sharpens the `requires` / `provides` tuple types so the coverage check and builder can read them precisely. Here a **provider** sets up a counter in `setup`, and a **consumer** reads it in a hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\n// Provider: declares `provides` and provisions the value in `setup`.\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\n// Consumer: declares `requires` and reads the value via `get` in a hook.\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n  onFinish(ctx) {\n    console.log(`Saw ${getCounter(ctx).value} chunks`);\n  },\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  // Provider must come before the consumer.\n  middleware: [withCounter, countsChunks],\n});\n```\n\nIf you drop `withCounter` from the array, `chat()` reports a compile-time error at the `middleware` option naming the missing `\"counter\"` capability — and throws at runtime before the adapter is ever called.\n\n### Builder example\n\n`createChatMiddleware()` builds the array through chained `.use()` calls and enforces **provider-before-consumer ordering at compile time**: each `.use()` requires that the middleware's `requires` are already covered by capabilities provided by earlier `.use()` calls.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n});\n\nconst middleware = createChatMiddleware()\n  .use(withCounter) // provides \"counter\"\n  .use(countsChunks) // requires \"counter\" — OK, already provided above\n  .build();\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware,\n});\n```\n\nSwap the two `.use()` calls (`.use(countsChunks).use(withCounter)`) and the builder rejects it at the `.use(countsChunks)` line — the consumer is ordered before its provider, so `\"counter\"` isn't in the provided set yet.\n\n### Validation guarantees\n\nThe capability system fails loudly and early:\n\n- **Compile-time coverage.** A required capability that nothing provides surfaces as a type error at the `middleware` option. This is enforced two ways: an **array coverage check** on `middleware: [...]`, and the order-aware **`createChatMiddleware()` builder** (which additionally enforces ordering).\n- **Runtime coverage.** Even if types are bypassed, `chat()` validates coverage and **throws before the adapter runs** if a required capability is missing.\n- **Post-`setup` assertion.** If a middleware declares a capability in `provides` but never calls its `provide` accessor during `setup`, `chat()` throws after the setup phase — you can't silently forget to provision.\n- **Duplicate provide → last-wins + warning.** If two middleware provide the same capability, the last write wins and a development warning is emitted.\n- **Unique names.** Capability `name`s must be unique across your app; the compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference).\n\n## Built-in Middleware\n\nTanStack AI ships ready-made middleware for common cases — caching tool results, redacting streamed text, and OpenTelemetry tracing:\n\n| Middleware | Import | What it does |\n|------------|--------|--------------|\n| `toolCacheMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Cache tool-call results by name + arguments |\n| `contentGuardMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Redact / transform / block streamed text content |\n| `otelMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` | Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics |\n\nSee [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware) for full options and examples for each. The recipes below show how to build your own.\n\n## Recipes\n\n### Live custom events\n\nA long `onConfig` hook can send progress to the client while it waits. Call `ctx.emitCustomEvent` when the work starts, then again when it finishes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:started\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:ended\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe engine yields each `CUSTOM` chunk as soon as you call `emitCustomEvent`. If `RUN_STARTED` is not on the wire yet, the engine sends it first. Durability then flushes the event so the client can render a live indicator. Read these events on the client the same way as tool `emitCustomEvent` calls. See [Custom Events](../protocol/custom-events).\n\n### Rate Limiting\n\nLimit the number of tool calls per request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(maxCalls: number): ChatMiddleware {\n  let toolCallCount = 0;\n  return {\n    name: \"rate-limit\",\n    onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n      toolCallCount++;\n      if (toolCallCount > maxCalls) {\n        return {\n          type: \"abort\",\n          reason: `Rate limit: exceeded ${maxCalls} tool calls`,\n        };\n      }\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### Audit Trail\n\nLog every action for compliance:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditTrail: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"audit-trail\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_started\",\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"tool_executed\",\n        toolName: info.toolName,\n        success: info.ok,\n        duration: info.duration,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_finished\",\n        duration: info.duration,\n        tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Per-Iteration Tool Swapping\n\nExpose different tools at different stages of the agent loop:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolSwapper: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-swapper\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n\n    if (ctx.iteration === 0) {\n      // First iteration: only allow search\n      return {\n        tools: config.tools.filter((t) => t.name === \"search\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Later iterations: allow all tools\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Content Filtering\n\nDrop or transform chunks before they reach the consumer:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { containsProfanity } from \"./filters\";\n\nconst contentFilter: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"content-filter\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      if (containsProfanity(chunk.delta)) {\n        // Drop the chunk entirely\n        return null;\n      }\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Error Recovery with Retry Logging\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { alertService } from \"./services\";\n\nconst errorRecovery: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"error-recovery\",\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      alertService.send({\n        level: \"error\",\n        message: `Chat ${ctx.requestId} failed after ${info.duration}ms`,\n        error: String(info.error),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## TypeScript Types\n\nThe core middleware types are exported from `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  ChatMiddleware,\n  ChatMiddlewareContext,\n  ChatMiddlewarePhase,\n  ChatMiddlewareConfig,\n  StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig,\n  ToolCallHookContext,\n  BeforeToolCallDecision,\n  AfterToolCallInfo,\n  IterationInfo,\n  ToolPhaseCompleteInfo,\n  UsageInfo,\n  FinishInfo,\n  AbortInfo,\n  ErrorInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n```\n\nThe option/type surfaces for the [built-in middleware](./built-in-middleware) are exported from the `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` subpath (not the main barrel):\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  ToolCacheMiddlewareOptions,\n  ToolCacheStorage,\n  ToolCacheEntry,\n  ContentGuardMiddlewareOptions,\n  ContentGuardRule,\n  ContentFilteredInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware) — `toolCacheMiddleware`, `contentGuardMiddleware`, `otelMiddleware`\n- [Compaction](./compaction): keep long chats under the context limit with `withCompaction`\n- [OpenTelemetry](./otel) — emit traces and metrics via `otelMiddleware`- [Tools](../tools/tools) — Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Agentic Cycle](../chat/agentic-cycle) — Understand the multi-step agent loop\n- [Streaming](../chat/streaming) — How streaming works in TanStack AI\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Middleware\nid: middleware\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Hook into every stage of TanStack AI's chat() lifecycle with middleware — logging, analytics, stream transforms, tool interception, and side effects.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - middleware\n  - chat middleware\n  - lifecycle hooks\n  - observability\n  - logging\n  - tool interception\n  - stream transform\n---\n\nMiddleware lets you hook into every stage of the `chat()` lifecycle — from configuration to streaming, tool execution, usage tracking, and completion. You can observe, transform, or short-circuit behavior at each stage without modifying your adapter or tool implementations.\n\nCommon use cases include:\n\n- **Logging and observability** — track token usage, tool execution timing, errors\n- **Configuration transforms** — inject system prompts, adjust temperature per iteration, filter tools\n- **Stream processing** — redact sensitive content, transform chunks, drop unwanted events\n- **Tool call interception** — validate arguments, cache results, abort on dangerous calls\n- **Side effects** — send analytics, update databases, trigger notifications\n\n## Quick Start\n\nPass an array of middleware to the `chat()` function:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst logger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"logger\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Chat started`);\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`[${ctx.requestId}] Finished in ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [logger],\n});\n```\n\n> **Just want to see chunks flowing through your middleware during development?**\n> Use `debug: { middleware: true }` on your `chat()` call — no custom middleware required. See [Debug Logging](./debug-logging).\n\n## Lifecycle Overview\n\nEvery `chat()` invocation follows a predictable lifecycle. Middleware hooks fire at specific phases:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"chat() called\"] --> B[\"onConfig (phase: init)\"]\n    B --> C[onStart]\n    C --> D[\"onConfig (phase: beforeModel)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Adapter streams response\"]\n    E --> F[\"onChunk (for each chunk)\"]\n    F --> G{Tool calls?}\n    G -->|No| H[onUsage]\n    G -->|Yes| I[onBeforeToolCall]\n    I --> J[Tool executes]\n    J --> K[onAfterToolCall]\n    K --> L{Continue loop?}\n    L -->|Yes| D\n    L -->|No| H\n    H --> SO{\"Structured output path?\"}\n    SO -->|None| M{Outcome}\n    SO -->|\"Native combined\"| SOH[\"Post-loop structured-output harvest (onChunk)\"]\n    SOH --> M\n    SO -->|\"Separate finalization\"| SOC[onStructuredOutputConfig]\n    SOC --> SOM[\"onConfig (phase: structuredOutput)\"]\n    SOM --> SOS[\"Structured-output finalization (onChunk, onUsage)\"]\n    SOS --> M\n    M -->|Success| N[onFinish]\n    M -->|Abort| O[onAbort]\n    M -->|Error| P[onError]\n\n    style I fill:#e1f5ff\n    style J fill:#ffe1e1\n    style SOC fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOM fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOS fill:#e1f5ff\n    style SOH fill:#e1f5ff\n    style N fill:#e1ffe1\n    style O fill:#fff4e1\n    style P fill:#ffe1e1\n```\n\n### Phase Transitions\n\nThe context's `phase` field tracks where you are in the lifecycle:\n\n| Phase | When | Hooks Called |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `init` | Once at startup | `onConfig` |\n| `beforeModel` | Before each model call (per iteration) | `onConfig` |\n| `modelStream` | While adapter streams chunks | `onChunk`, `onUsage` |\n| `beforeTools` | Before tool execution | `onBeforeToolCall` |\n| `afterTools` | After tool execution | `onAfterToolCall` |\n| `structuredOutput` | During the final structured-output adapter call (when `outputSchema` is set **and** `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options). Chunks from `adapter.structuredOutputStream` (or the synthesized non-streaming fallback) flow through `onChunk` with this phase, and `onUsage` fires for the final call's tokens. **Does not fire** for adapters that natively combine tools + schema in one streaming call (modern OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x family, and OpenRouter when every routed model is in `OPENROUTER_COMBINED_TOOLS_AND_SCHEMA_MODELS`; see issue #605). On that path middleware observes the run through `beforeModel` / `modelStream` as usual. | `onStructuredOutputConfig`, `onConfig`, `onChunk`, `onUsage` |\n\n## Hooks Reference\n\n### onConfig\n\nCalled once during `init` (startup) and once per iteration during `beforeModel` (before each model call). On the separate-finalization path, `onConfig` additionally re-fires at the structured-output boundary with `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'`, receiving the post-`onStructuredOutputConfig` view of the config. A single-iteration separate-finalization run therefore fires `onConfig` three times (`init` + `beforeModel` + `structuredOutput`). Native-combined output does not add this third call. Use `onConfig` to transform the configuration that the model receives.\n\nReturn a **partial** config object with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config automatically. No need to spread the existing config.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst dynamicTemperature: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"dynamic-temperature\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase === \"init\") {\n      // Add a system prompt at startup — only systemPrompts is overwritten\n      return {\n        systemPrompts: [\n          ...config.systemPrompts,\n          \"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n        ],\n      };\n    }\n\n    if (ctx.phase === \"beforeModel\" && ctx.iteration > 0) {\n      // Increase temperature on retries. Sampling params live in the\n      // provider-native modelOptions object — `temperature` is universal,\n      // so it's the same key across providers. Spread the existing\n      // modelOptions so other model options stay unchanged.\n      const current =\n        typeof config.modelOptions?.temperature === \"number\"\n          ? config.modelOptions.temperature\n          : 0.7;\n      return {\n        modelOptions: {\n          ...config.modelOptions,\n          temperature: Math.min(current + 0.1, 1.0),\n        },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n> Sampling parameters (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the various `max*Tokens` keys) live inside `modelOptions` under each provider's native name — they are no longer root config fields. `temperature` happens to be spelled the same across every provider, so the example above is provider-agnostic; if you mutate a token limit instead, use the provider-native key (e.g. `max_output_tokens` for OpenAI, `num_predict` nested under `modelOptions.options` for Ollama). See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n**Config fields you can transform:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `messages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Canonical conversation history. Persistence and `ctx.messages` use this field. |\n| `providerMessages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Temporary context sent to the provider. Defaults to `messages`. |\n| `systemPrompts` | `string[]` | System prompts |\n| `tools` | `Tool[]` | Available tools |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Request metadata |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Provider-native options — this is where sampling params (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the provider's `max*Tokens` key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options). |\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onConfig`, the config is **piped** through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware.\n\nReturn `providerMessages` when a transform must affect only the model call. For\ncompatibility, returning `messages` also updates provider input unless the same\nresult sets `providerMessages` explicitly.\n\n### onStructuredOutputConfig\n\nCalled once at the start of the final structured-output adapter call — only when `chat()` was invoked with `outputSchema` **and** `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options. Pipes through middleware in order, like `onConfig`, but with access to the **JSON Schema** being sent to the provider. Use this hook when you need to transform the schema (e.g., inject `$defs`, strip vendor-incompatible keywords) or apply structured-output-specific behavior (e.g., suppress system prompts on the final call).\n\n> Native-combined adapters (modern OpenAI, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605) skip the separate finalization call and never invoke this hook. The engine passes the converted schema directly to `chatStream` after `onConfig` runs, so middleware cannot transform the native-combined schema.\n\nReturn a **partial** `StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig` with only the fields you want to change — they are shallow-merged with the current config. Return `void` to pass through.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { sharedDefs } from \"./defs\";\n\nconst injectDefs: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"inject-defs\",\n  onStructuredOutputConfig: (_ctx, config) => {\n    // `config.outputSchema` is the JSON Schema being sent to the provider\n    return {\n      outputSchema: {\n        ...config.outputSchema,\n        $defs: { ...sharedDefs },\n      },\n    };\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Config fields you can transform:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `messages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Canonical conversation history |\n| `providerMessages` | `ModelMessage[]` | Temporary context sent to the final call |\n| `systemPrompts` | `SystemPrompt[]` | System prompts on the final call |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Request metadata |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Provider-native options — this is where sampling params (`temperature`, `top_p` / `topP`, the provider's `max*Tokens` key) now live, alongside every other model-specific knob. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options). |\n| `outputSchema` | `JSONSchema` | JSON Schema being sent to the provider for structured output |\n\n**Ordering at the structured-output boundary:**\n\n1. `onStructuredOutputConfig` fires first, piping through every middleware in array order.\n2. `onConfig` then re-fires at the same boundary with `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'`, receiving the post-`onStructuredOutputConfig` view of the config (minus `outputSchema`). Use `onConfig` for general-purpose transforms that apply to every adapter call; use `onStructuredOutputConfig` when you need access to the schema.\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onStructuredOutputConfig`, the config is **piped** through them in order — each receives the merged config from the previous middleware.\n\n### onStart\n\nCalled once after the initial `onConfig` completes. Use it for setup tasks like initializing timers or logging.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timer: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timer\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    console.log(`Request ${ctx.requestId} started at iteration ${ctx.iteration}`);\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### onChunk\n\nCalled for every chunk streamed from the adapter. You can observe, transform, expand, or drop chunks.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactor: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redactor\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      // Transform: redact sensitive content\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Return void to pass through unchanged\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Return values:**\n\n| Return | Effect |\n|--------|--------|\n| `void` / `undefined` | Chunk passes through unchanged |\n| `StreamChunk` | Replaces the original chunk |\n| `StreamChunk[]` | Expands into multiple chunks |\n| `null` | Drops the chunk entirely |\n\nWhen multiple middleware define `onChunk`, chunks flow through them in order. If one middleware drops a chunk (returns `null`), subsequent middleware never see it.\n\n#### Chunk types you'll see\n\n`onChunk` receives every [AG-UI event](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) the run produces — not just text. Narrow on `chunk.type` (a discriminated union) before reading type-specific fields. The common ones:\n\n| `chunk.type` | Meaning | Key fields |\n|--------------|---------|-----------|\n| `RUN_STARTED` / `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERROR` | Run lifecycle boundaries | `runId`, `finishReason`, `usage` (on finish), `message` (on error) |\n| `TEXT_MESSAGE_START` / `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` / `TEXT_MESSAGE_END` | Assistant text streaming | `messageId`, `delta` (content) |\n| `TOOL_CALL_START` / `TOOL_CALL_ARGS` / `TOOL_CALL_END` | Tool invocation streaming | `toolCallId`, `toolCallName`, `delta` (args), result on end |\n| `STEP_STARTED` / `STEP_FINISHED` | Thinking / reasoning steps | `delta`, `signature` |\n| `STATE_SNAPSHOT` / `STATE_DELTA` | Agent state sync | `snapshot`, `delta` |\n| `CUSTOM` | Extensibility events (incl. structured-output — see below) | `name`, `value` |\n\nSee the [AG-UI protocol docs](https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction) for the full event catalogue and exact field shapes.\n\n#### Transforming structured-output chunks\n\nThere is **no separate `onStructuredOutputChunk` hook** — and you don't need one. When `chat()` is invoked with `outputSchema`, the structured-output chunks (the JSON `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` deltas, plus the `structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM events and any finalization `RUN_ERROR`) flow through the **same `onChunk` hook** as everything else. You transform, expand, or drop them exactly like any other chunk.\n\nHow you distinguish them depends on which finalization path the adapter takes:\n\n- **Separate-finalization adapters** (`supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema()` does not return `true` for the current model/options): `ctx.phase === 'structuredOutput'` during the finalization call. Discriminate on the phase.\n- **Native-combined adapters** (modern OpenAI Chat Completions / Responses, Claude 4.5+, Gemini 3.x, Grok 4.x — see issue #605): the schema-constrained JSON is produced on the model's natural final turn, so **`ctx.phase` stays `'modelStream'`** — the `'structuredOutput'` phase never fires. Discriminate on the CUSTOM event name (`structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete`) instead.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst redactStructuredOutput: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"redact-structured-output\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    // Separate-finalization path: the JSON streams as TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\n    // during the 'structuredOutput' phase. Transform the delta like any\n    // other text chunk — here, redact anything that looks like an SSN before\n    // it reaches the client.\n    if (\n      ctx.phase === \"structuredOutput\" &&\n      chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"\n    ) {\n      return {\n        ...chunk,\n        delta: chunk.delta.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[REDACTED]\"),\n      };\n    }\n\n    // Both paths: the completed typed payload arrives as a CUSTOM\n    // `structured-output.complete` event. On the native-combined path this is\n    // your only signal (ctx.phase never flips to 'structuredOutput'), so key\n    // off the event name, not the phase. `chunk.value` carries { object, raw }.\n    if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n      console.log(\"final structured output:\", chunk.value);\n    }\n\n    // Return void to pass everything else through unchanged.\n  },\n};\n```\n\n> Why is there `onStructuredOutputConfig` but no `onStructuredOutputChunk`? Because the **config** shape genuinely differs at the structured-output boundary — it carries an `outputSchema` field that plain `ChatMiddlewareConfig` doesn't (see [onStructuredOutputConfig](#onstructuredoutputconfig)). **Chunks** are all just `StreamChunk` regardless of phase, so one `onChunk` plus `ctx.phase` (or the CUSTOM event name) covers every case — a parallel chunk hook would be redundant.\n\n### onShouldContinue\n\nCalled when the engine is deciding whether to start another agent-loop iteration (after a tool phase or between model turns). Combined with AND semantics across middleware **and** with `agentLoopStrategy` — any explicit `false` stops the loop. Return `true`, `void`, or `undefined` to allow continuation.\n\nDoes **not** abort the run: the stream finishes normally with the current messages. Use `ctx.abort()` only for a hard abort.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst budget: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-budget\",\n  onShouldContinue: (_ctx, state) => {\n    // Stop further turns once 20 tool calls have been emitted\n    if (state.toolCallCount >= 20) return false;\n  },\n};\n```\n\nFor a full per-turn + cumulative tool budget recipe, see [Tool-call budgets](../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe).\n\n### onInterruptBoundary and onInterruptResolution\n\nUse these hooks when middleware needs data from the client. Define the request\nwith `defineInterrupt()` and register it with `chat({ interrupts })` and\n`useChat({ interrupts })`. Do not emit raw AG-UI events from middleware.\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` runs at four points in an agent iteration:\n\n- `beforeModel`, before the adapter starts.\n- `afterModel`, after the model response is complete.\n- `beforeTools`, before tool execution starts.\n- `afterTools`, after the tool phase is complete.\n\nEach middleware can return requests from one boundary. The engine combines all\nrequests from that boundary into one AG-UI interrupt batch. The batch ends the\nrun with one interrupt outcome.\n\nThis hook cannot change config. Its only legal return is `{ interrupts }` or\nnothing. The continuation is a new `chat()` call, so the hook runs again. Skip\nthe emit when `ctx.parentRunId` is set if this pause belongs to the original\nrequest only.\n\nWhat is in `ctx` at each phase, and when to use each phase, is in\n[Lifecycle Boundaries](../interrupts/boundaries).\n\nCreate one shared definition. Both the server and the client import this value,\nso the definition ID and response shape stay the same on both sides.\n\n```typescript title=\"review-plan.ts\"\nimport { defineInterrupt, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const reviewPlan = defineInterrupt({\n  id: 'review-plan',\n  payloadSchema: z.object({ title: z.string() }),\n  responseSchema: z.object({ approved: z.boolean() }),\n})\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeTools') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'release-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Approve this plan?',\n          payload: { title: 'Release plan' },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nRegister the definition on the server. Forward `parentRunId` and `resume` so\na client resolution starts the continuation with its full context.\n\n```typescript title=\"route.ts\"\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequestBody,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware, reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequestBody(await request.json())\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nRegister the same definition on the client. Check `kind` and `definitionId`.\nTypeScript then treats the item as `GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>`.\n`resolveInterrupt` uses the response shape from `reviewPlan.responseSchema`.\n\n```tsx title=\"review-plan-panel.tsx\"\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { GenericInterrupt } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './review-plan'\n\nfunction ReviewCard({\n  interrupt,\n}: {\n  interrupt: GenericInterrupt<typeof reviewPlan>\n}) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt({ approved: true })}\n    >\n      Approve plan\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n\nexport function ReviewPlanPanel() {\n  const { interrupts, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button onClick={() => sendMessage('Review the release plan')}>\n        Start review\n      </button>\n      {interrupts.map((interrupt) => {\n        if (interrupt.kind !== 'generic') return null\n        if (!('definitionId' in interrupt)) return null\n        if (interrupt.definitionId !== reviewPlan.id) return null\n        return <ReviewCard key={interrupt.id} interrupt={interrupt} />\n      })}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`onInterruptResolution` does not run in the `chat()` call that paused. It\nruns once at the start of the next `chat()` call, after the client answers.\n\n```\nsetup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop\n```\n\n`useChat` sends `parentRunId` and `resume` on that second request. Each\ngeneric resume item includes the original request in `metadata`. If `resume`\nis present and `parentRunId` is missing, the server throws.\n\nUse `resumedInterrupts.for(definition)` for one typed definition. Use\n`resumedInterrupts.all()` for every registered definition. Use\n`resumedInterrupts.all(definitionA, definitionB)` to read a typed subset.\n\nThe hook can return `toolResume: 'continue'`, `'cancel'`, or `'stop'`. Results\nfrom all middleware combine by the most restrictive rule: `stop` wins over\n`cancel`, and `cancel` wins over `continue`.\n\nThis hook cannot change prompts, tools, or messages. Store the answer on a\ncapability, then return those fields from `onConfig` when\n`ctx.phase === 'beforeModel'`.\n\n| Hook | Can change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `onInterruptBoundary` | Nothing. It can only pause. |\n| `onInterruptResolution` | Pending-tool policy (`toolResume`) |\n| `onConfig` | `messages`, `systemPrompts`, `tools`, `modelOptions`, `metadata` |\n\nThe full resume order, plus an example that writes a user note into the\nsystem prompt, is in [Apply Answers](../interrupts/apply-answers).\n\n### onBeforeToolCall\n\nCalled before each tool executes. The first middleware that returns a non-void decision short-circuits — remaining middleware are skipped for that tool call.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction isRecord(v: unknown): v is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof v === \"object\" && v !== null;\n}\n\nconst guard: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"guard\",\n  onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n    // Block dangerous tools\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"deleteDatabase\") {\n      return { type: \"abort\", reason: \"Dangerous operation blocked\" };\n    }\n\n    // Validate and transform arguments\n    if (hookCtx.toolName === \"search\" && isRecord(hookCtx.args) && !hookCtx.args.limit) {\n      return {\n        type: \"transformArgs\",\n        args: { ...hookCtx.args, limit: 10 },\n      };\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Decision types:**\n\n| Decision | Effect |\n|----------|--------|\n| `void` / `undefined` | Continue normally, next middleware can decide |\n| `{ type: 'transformArgs', args }` | Replace tool arguments before execution |\n| `{ type: 'skip', result }` | Skip execution entirely, use provided result |\n| `{ type: 'abort', reason? }` | Abort the entire chat run |\n\nThe `hookCtx` provides:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `toolCall` | `ToolCall` | Raw tool call object |\n| `tool` | `Tool \\| undefined` | Resolved tool definition |\n| `args` | `unknown` | Parsed arguments |\n| `toolName` | `string` | Tool name |\n| `toolCallId` | `string` | Tool call ID |\n\n### onAfterToolCall\n\nCalled after each tool execution (or skip). All middleware run — there is no short-circuiting.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolLogger: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-logger\",\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    if (info.ok) {\n      console.log(`${info.toolName} completed in ${info.duration}ms`);\n    } else {\n      console.error(`${info.toolName} failed:`, info.error);\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `info` object provides:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `toolCall` | `ToolCall` | Raw tool call object |\n| `tool` | `Tool \\| undefined` | Resolved tool definition |\n| `toolName` | `string` | Tool name |\n| `toolCallId` | `string` | Tool call ID |\n| `ok` | `boolean` | Whether execution succeeded |\n| `duration` | `number` | Execution time in milliseconds |\n| `result` | `unknown` | Result (when `ok` is true) |\n| `error` | `unknown` | Error (when `ok` is false) |\n\n### Tool hook order in one turn\n\nWhen the model calls several server tools in one turn, the tools run at the same time:\n\n- `onBeforeToolCall` runs for each call in call order, before any tool starts.\n- `onAfterToolCall` runs for each tool when it finishes, so in finish order.\n- A call that `onBeforeToolCall` skips gets its `onAfterToolCall` right away, before the tools start.\n- If the run aborts before the tools start, no tool runs. Each call gets `onAfterToolCall` with `ok: false` and the error \"Operation aborted\".\n- If `onBeforeToolCall` aborts or throws for a call, the calls before it still run. The error is thrown after they finish.\n\nWith `toolExecution: 'sequential'`, each call finishes its `onBeforeToolCall`, its run, and its `onAfterToolCall` before the next call starts. See [Run tools one at a time](../tools/tools#run-tools-one-at-a-time).\n\n### onUsage\n\nCalled once per model iteration when the `RUN_FINISHED` chunk includes usage data. Receives the usage object directly.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst usageTracker: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"usage-tracker\",\n  onUsage: (ctx, usage) => {\n    console.log(\n      `Iteration ${ctx.iteration}: ${usage.totalTokens} tokens`\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `usage` object:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `promptTokens` | `number` | Input tokens |\n| `completionTokens` | `number` | Output tokens |\n| `totalTokens` | `number` | Total tokens |\n\n### Terminal Hooks: onFinish, onAbort, onError\n\nExactly **one** terminal hook fires per `chat()` invocation. They are mutually exclusive:\n\n| Hook | When it fires |\n|------|--------------|\n| `onFinish` | Run completed normally |\n| `onAbort` | Run was aborted (via `ctx.abort()`, an external `AbortSignal`, or a `{ type: 'abort' }` decision from `onBeforeToolCall`) |\n| `onError` | An unhandled error occurred |\n\n`onFinish` also fires when the invocation pauses at a client-tool or approval wait. The run is not complete yet. To tell a pause from a completion, look in `onChunk` for a `RUN_FINISHED` chunk with `outcome.type === 'interrupt'`.\n\n> **Separate-finalization path:** Adapters without native-combined support make a separate structured-output provider call after the agent loop.\n>\n> - `onStructuredOutputConfig` fires before the separate provider call, and `ctx.phase` is `'structuredOutput'` for its chunks.\n> - `onIteration` does **not** fire for finalization; it only fires for agent-loop iterations.\n> - `onFinish` fires after finalization completes. Its `info` object reflects the **agent loop's** terminal state.\n> - `info.content` — the agent loop's accumulated text. Separate-finalization JSON deltas are **not** included. Middleware can observe the completed result through the `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM event in `onChunk`.\n> - `info.usage` — the agent loop's last `RUN_FINISHED.usage`. For a tools-less structured-output run (no agent-loop iteration produces `RUN_FINISHED`), this is `undefined`. To capture finalization tokens, use `onUsage` — that hook fires for **every** `RUN_FINISHED` carrying usage, including the finalization call.\n> - `info.finishReason` — the agent loop's last `finishReason`. `null` when no agent-loop iteration produced `RUN_FINISHED` (e.g. a tools-less structured-output run).\n> - `info.duration` — wall-clock duration of the entire `chat()` invocation, including finalization.\n>\n> **Native-combined output:** Adapters with native-combined support produce the schema-constrained JSON in the regular agent-loop stream. `onStructuredOutputConfig` does not fire, `ctx.phase` remains `'modelStream'`, and `onIteration` fires for the iteration that produces the JSON. The JSON is agent-loop text, so `info.content` includes it. Middleware observes the `structured-output.complete` event in `onChunk` during the same phase.\n>\n> On successful completion in either path, `onFinish` receives the complete canonical transcript in `ctx.messages`. Native-combined output keeps the structured result on its terminal assistant message. The separate-finalization path can preserve the agent loop's plain-text assistant message followed by a distinct structured-output assistant message. This transcript is separate from the path-specific fields on `info`.\n>\n> To aggregate usage across the whole run, accumulate from `onUsage` callbacks rather than relying on `info.usage`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst terminal: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"terminal\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Finished: ${info.finishReason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n    console.log(`Content: ${info.content}`);\n    if (info.usage) {\n      console.log(`Tokens: ${info.usage.totalTokens}`);\n    }\n  },\n  onAbort: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.log(`Aborted: ${info.reason}, ${info.duration}ms`);\n  },\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    console.error(`Error after ${info.duration}ms:`, info.error);\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe `info` object for `onFinish` (`FinishInfo`):\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `finishReason` | `string \\| null` | The agent loop's last `finishReason`. `null` when no agent-loop iteration produced `RUN_FINISHED` (e.g. a tools-less `chat({ outputSchema })` run). |\n| `duration` | `number` | Total run duration in milliseconds, including any structured-output finalization. |\n| `content` | `string` | The agent loop's accumulated text content. Includes native-combined structured JSON; excludes separate-finalization JSON. Observe the completed result through the `structured-output.complete` CUSTOM event via `onChunk`. |\n| `usage` | `{ promptTokens; completionTokens; totalTokens } \\| undefined` | **Optional.** The agent loop's last `RUN_FINISHED.usage`. **Does not include finalization tokens** — use `onUsage` to observe those. Always guard with `if (info.usage)` or `info.usage?.`. |\n\n## Context Object\n\nEvery hook receives a `ChatMiddlewareContext` as its first argument. It provides request-scoped information and control functions:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `requestId` | `string` | Unique ID for this chat request |\n| `streamId` | `string` | Unique ID for this stream |\n| `threadId` | `string` | AG-UI thread identifier. Resolves to caller-provided `threadId` (or legacy `conversationId`), or an auto-generated value if neither is supplied. Use this for event correlation. |\n| `conversationId` | `string \\| undefined` | **Deprecated** alias of `threadId`. Always equals `ctx.threadId`; retained so middleware written before the AG-UI rename keeps working. New middleware should read `ctx.threadId`. |\n| `phase` | `ChatMiddlewarePhase` | Current lifecycle phase |\n| `iteration` | `number` | Agent loop iteration (0-indexed) |\n| `chunkIndex` | `number` | Running count of chunks yielded |\n| `signal` | `AbortSignal \\| undefined` | External abort signal |\n| `abort(reason?)` | `function` | Abort the run from within middleware |\n| `emitCustomEvent(name, value, options?)` | `function` | Push a `CUSTOM` chunk onto the chat stream now. The engine yields it while the current hook is still running, including during `onConfig`. Durability flushes it immediately. Pass `{ batch: true }` to keep it in the durability batch. |\n| `context` | `TContext` | User-provided runtime context value |\n| `defer(promise)` | `function` | Register a non-blocking side-effect |\n\n## Typed Runtime Context\n\n`ChatMiddleware` accepts a context generic. This lets reusable middleware declared outside `chat()` access the same typed runtime context as your tools.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { session, audit } from \"./server\";\n\ntype AppContext = {\n  userId: string;\n  audit: {\n    write(event: { userId: string; requestId: string }): Promise<void>;\n  };\n};\n\nexport const auditMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<AppContext> = {\n  name: \"audit\",\n  onStart(ctx) {\n    ctx.defer(\n      ctx.context.audit.write({\n        userId: ctx.context.userId,\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [auditMiddleware],\n  context: {\n    userId: session.user.id,\n    audit,\n  },\n});\n```\n\nWhen typed middleware or typed tools are present, `chat()` checks that the provided `context` matches the required shape. Existing middleware typed as plain `ChatMiddleware` still works; its `ctx.context` remains `unknown` and does not force a `context` option.\n\nRuntime context is process-local application state. It is separate from AG-UI `RunAgentInput.context`, which is protocol metadata parsed by `chatParamsFromRequest`. See [Runtime Context](./runtime-context) for server, client, and client-to-server handoff patterns.\n\n### Aborting from Middleware\n\nCall `ctx.abort()` to gracefully stop the run. This triggers the `onAbort` terminal hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst timeout: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"timeout\",\n  onChunk: (ctx) => {\n    if (ctx.chunkIndex > 1000) {\n      ctx.abort(\"Too many chunks\");\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Deferred Side Effects\n\nUse `ctx.defer()` to register promises that run after the terminal hook without blocking the stream:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst analytics: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"analytics\",\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      fetch(\"/api/analytics\", {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          requestId: ctx.requestId,\n          duration: info.duration,\n          tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        }),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Composing Multiple Middleware\n\nMiddleware execute in array order. The ordering matters for hooks that pipe or short-circuit:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware } from \"./middleware\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware: [authMiddleware, loggingMiddleware, cachingMiddleware],\n});\n```\n\n### Composition Rules\n\n| Hook | Composition | Effect of Order |\n|------|------------|----------------|\n| `onConfig` | **Piped** — each receives previous output | Earlier middleware transforms first |\n| `onStructuredOutputConfig` | **Piped** — each receives previous output | Earlier middleware transforms first |\n| `onStart` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onChunk` | **Piped** — chunks flow through each middleware | If first drops a chunk, later middleware never see it |\n| `onBeforeToolCall` | **First-win** — first non-void decision wins | Earlier middleware has priority |\n| `onShouldContinue` | **AND** — any explicit `false` stops the loop | Order only affects which middleware runs first when short-circuiting |\n| `onAfterToolCall` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onUsage` | Sequential | All run in order |\n| `onFinish/onAbort/onError` | Sequential | All run in order |\n\n## Capabilities\n\nMiddleware often need to **share state**. A provider middleware sets something up (a database handle, a per-request counter, a sandbox), and a consumer middleware reads it back later in the same run. Capabilities make that hand-off **type-safe and order-checked**: the consumer declares what it needs, the provider declares what it offers, and `chat()` refuses to run (at compile time _and_ at runtime) if a required capability was never provided.\n\n### Creating a capability\n\nA capability is created with `createCapability<TValue>()('name')` — a **curried** call:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCapability } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n```\n\nThe currying is deliberate: you supply the **value type** explicitly (`<{ value: number }>`) while the **name literal** is inferred from the argument (`\"counter\"`). A single `createCapability<T>('name')` call can't do both — supplying `T` explicitly stops TypeScript inferring the name, collapsing it to `string` and defeating the compile-time coverage check that keys on the literal name.\n\nThe returned `counterCapability` is a hybrid value:\n\n- It **destructures to `[get, provide]`** — the two accessors you use inside hooks.\n- It **is itself the identity** you list in `requires` / `provides`. There is no separate token to import.\n\nThe accessors:\n\n| Accessor | Behavior |\n|----------|----------|\n| `getCounter(ctx)` | Returns the value. **Throws** if the capability was never provided. |\n| `getCounter(ctx, { optional: true })` | Returns `TValue \\| undefined` — no throw when absent. |\n| `provideCounter(ctx, value)` | Sets the value for this run. Call it from `setup`. |\n\nEquivalently, the context exposes `ctx.get(capability)`, `ctx.getOptional(capability)`, and `ctx.provide(capability, value)` — pass the capability handle directly. These are typed by the handle you pass (`ctx.get(counterCapability)` returns the value type), so `getCounter(ctx)` and `ctx.get(counterCapability)` are interchangeable — use whichever reads better in your hook.\n\n> **Capability names must be unique across your app.** The compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference), so two capabilities sharing a name will conflate in the type-level check.\n\n### The `setup` hook\n\nProvisioning happens in a dedicated `setup(ctx)` hook. It **runs first** — before any `onConfig` (init), across all middleware in array order — so that by the time the rest of the lifecycle begins, every capability is in place. `setup` receives the stable `ChatMiddlewareContext` (not the mutable config), and may be async.\n\n### `requires` / `provides` / `optionalRequires`\n\nThree array fields on a middleware declare its capability contract. Each is a `ReadonlyArray<CapabilityHandle>` — you list the capability handles themselves:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `provides` | Capabilities this middleware sets up. Each one **must** be `provide`d inside `setup`, or `chat()` throws after the setup phase. |\n| `requires` | Capabilities this middleware reads. `chat()` validates (compile time + runtime) that some earlier middleware provides each one. |\n| `optionalRequires` | Capabilities used **if present** but not required. Non-gating — never causes a validation error. Read with `getX(ctx, { optional: true })`. |\n\n### Array example\n\nAuthor middleware with `defineChatMiddleware` — it sharpens the `requires` / `provides` tuple types so the coverage check and builder can read them precisely. Here a **provider** sets up a counter in `setup`, and a **consumer** reads it in a hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\n// Provider: declares `provides` and provisions the value in `setup`.\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\n// Consumer: declares `requires` and reads the value via `get` in a hook.\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n  onFinish(ctx) {\n    console.log(`Saw ${getCounter(ctx).value} chunks`);\n  },\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  // Provider must come before the consumer.\n  middleware: [withCounter, countsChunks],\n});\n```\n\nIf you drop `withCounter` from the array, `chat()` reports a compile-time error at the `middleware` option naming the missing `\"counter\"` capability — and throws at runtime before the adapter is ever called.\n\n### Builder example\n\n`createChatMiddleware()` builds the array through chained `.use()` calls and enforces **provider-before-consumer ordering at compile time**: each `.use()` requires that the middleware's `requires` are already covered by capabilities provided by earlier `.use()` calls.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  createCapability,\n  createChatMiddleware,\n  defineChatMiddleware,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst counterCapability = createCapability<{ value: number }>()(\"counter\");\nconst [getCounter, provideCounter] = counterCapability;\n\nconst withCounter = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"with-counter\",\n  provides: [counterCapability],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideCounter(ctx, { value: 0 });\n  },\n});\n\nconst countsChunks = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"counts-chunks\",\n  requires: [counterCapability],\n  onChunk(ctx) {\n    getCounter(ctx).value++;\n  },\n});\n\nconst middleware = createChatMiddleware()\n  .use(withCounter) // provides \"counter\"\n  .use(countsChunks) // requires \"counter\" — OK, already provided above\n  .build();\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  middleware,\n});\n```\n\nSwap the two `.use()` calls (`.use(countsChunks).use(withCounter)`) and the builder rejects it at the `.use(countsChunks)` line — the consumer is ordered before its provider, so `\"counter\"` isn't in the provided set yet.\n\n### Validation guarantees\n\nThe capability system fails loudly and early:\n\n- **Compile-time coverage.** A required capability that nothing provides surfaces as a type error at the `middleware` option. This is enforced two ways: an **array coverage check** on `middleware: [...]`, and the order-aware **`createChatMiddleware()` builder** (which additionally enforces ordering).\n- **Runtime coverage.** Even if types are bypassed, `chat()` validates coverage and **throws before the adapter runs** if a required capability is missing.\n- **Post-`setup` assertion.** If a middleware declares a capability in `provides` but never calls its `provide` accessor during `setup`, `chat()` throws after the setup phase — you can't silently forget to provision.\n- **Duplicate provide → last-wins + warning.** If two middleware provide the same capability, the last write wins and a development warning is emitted.\n- **Unique names.** Capability `name`s must be unique across your app; the compile-time coverage check keys on the name literal (runtime keys on the handle reference).\n\n## Built-in Middleware\n\nTanStack AI ships ready-made middleware for common cases — caching tool results, redacting streamed text, and OpenTelemetry tracing:\n\n| Middleware | Import | What it does |\n|------------|--------|--------------|\n| `toolCacheMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Cache tool-call results by name + arguments |\n| `contentGuardMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Redact / transform / block streamed text content |\n| `otelMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` | Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics |\n\nSee [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware) for full options and examples for each. The recipes below show how to build your own.\n\n## Recipes\n\n### Live custom events\n\nA long `onConfig` hook can send progress to the client while it waits. Call `ctx.emitCustomEvent` when the work starts, then again when it finishes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:started\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"job:ended\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThe engine yields each `CUSTOM` chunk as soon as you call `emitCustomEvent`. If `RUN_STARTED` is not on the wire yet, the engine sends it first. Durability then flushes the event so the client can render a live indicator. Read these events on the client the same way as tool `emitCustomEvent` calls. See [Custom Events](../protocol/custom-events).\n\n### Rate Limiting\n\nLimit the number of tool calls per request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nfunction rateLimitMiddleware(maxCalls: number): ChatMiddleware {\n  let toolCallCount = 0;\n  return {\n    name: \"rate-limit\",\n    onBeforeToolCall: (ctx, hookCtx) => {\n      toolCallCount++;\n      if (toolCallCount > maxCalls) {\n        return {\n          type: \"abort\",\n          reason: `Rate limit: exceeded ${maxCalls} tool calls`,\n        };\n      }\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### Audit Trail\n\nLog every action for compliance:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditTrail: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"audit-trail\",\n  onStart: (ctx) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_started\",\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onAfterToolCall: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"tool_executed\",\n        toolName: info.toolName,\n        success: info.ok,\n        duration: info.duration,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n  onFinish: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      db.auditLog.create({\n        requestId: ctx.requestId,\n        event: \"chat_finished\",\n        duration: info.duration,\n        tokens: info.usage?.totalTokens,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Per-Iteration Tool Swapping\n\nExpose different tools at different stages of the agent loop:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst toolSwapper: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"tool-swapper\",\n  onConfig: (ctx, config) => {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n\n    if (ctx.iteration === 0) {\n      // First iteration: only allow search\n      return {\n        tools: config.tools.filter((t) => t.name === \"search\"),\n      };\n    }\n    // Later iterations: allow all tools\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Content Filtering\n\nDrop or transform chunks before they reach the consumer:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { containsProfanity } from \"./filters\";\n\nconst contentFilter: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"content-filter\",\n  onChunk: (ctx, chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\") {\n      if (containsProfanity(chunk.delta)) {\n        // Drop the chunk entirely\n        return null;\n      }\n    }\n  },\n};\n```\n\n### Error Recovery with Retry Logging\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { alertService } from \"./services\";\n\nconst errorRecovery: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"error-recovery\",\n  onError: (ctx, info) => {\n    ctx.defer(\n      alertService.send({\n        level: \"error\",\n        message: `Chat ${ctx.requestId} failed after ${info.duration}ms`,\n        error: String(info.error),\n      })\n    );\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## TypeScript Types\n\nThe core middleware types are exported from `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  ChatMiddleware,\n  ChatMiddlewareContext,\n  ChatMiddlewarePhase,\n  ChatMiddlewareConfig,\n  StructuredOutputMiddlewareConfig,\n  ToolCallHookContext,\n  BeforeToolCallDecision,\n  AfterToolCallInfo,\n  IterationInfo,\n  ToolPhaseCompleteInfo,\n  UsageInfo,\n  FinishInfo,\n  AbortInfo,\n  ErrorInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n```\n\nThe option/type surfaces for the [built-in middleware](./built-in-middleware) are exported from the `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` subpath (not the main barrel):\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  ToolCacheMiddlewareOptions,\n  ToolCacheStorage,\n  ToolCacheEntry,\n  ContentGuardMiddlewareOptions,\n  ContentGuardRule,\n  ContentFilteredInfo,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware) — `toolCacheMiddleware`, `contentGuardMiddleware`, `otelMiddleware`\n- [Compaction](./compaction): keep long chats under the context limit with `withCompaction`\n- [OpenTelemetry](./otel) — emit traces and metrics via `otelMiddleware`- [Tools](../tools/tools) — Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Agentic Cycle](../chat/agentic-cycle) — Understand the multi-step agent loop\n- [Streaming](../chat/streaming) — How streaming works in TanStack AI\n"}
